    "lesson": 22,
    "text1":
        "{r:I am going to visit the central city twice this week. My friend is going to be ready to go with me. We are going to see the clear sky. My parents are going to make some dinner for us}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:I am going to make a decision about my Future. My sister is going to help me think. My intention is clear. My parents are going to know my plans soon}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I am going to send the invitation today. My friends are going to come soon. I am going to arrange a big party. Maybe we are going to make an appointment for next week}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I am going to call the driver to take us to the city. My brother is going to sit in the car. We are going to see the central part. The driver knows exactly where to go. My parents are going to meet us there}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Talk with the Teacher[/center]\nChild: I am going to explain my intention in a very clear way.\nTeacher: I am going to listen to you. What is your intention?\nChild: I am sure you are going to ask many questions.\nTeacher: That is true. But your parents are going to be happy with your decision, I am sure.\nChild:Maybe(balki)"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 23,
    "text1":
        "{r:I will make some meat for dinner tomorrow. My sister will help me. We will probably invite our old friends. Our parents will come and tell us things}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:I will buy a new lamp for the room. My brother will help me. We will probably move some things there. Our friends will lend us some things from their house. Because i am poor and i dont have money even for bread}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I will make a trip for next weekend. My friends will probably come with me. We will visit a new place. My parents will know about our arrangement}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I will watch the game tomorrow. My sister will probably watch it too. We will wear our new jeans. But my mother says that i should be interested in science. Because it will make me famous and rich}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Lending a Book[/center]\nFriend A: I will lend you my book tomorrow.\nFriend B: Thank you! I will probably give it back next week.\nFriend A: Good. We will talk about the book then.\nFriend B: Yes, I think it is a good book and i will learn much from the book."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 24,
    "text1":
        "{r:I will not eat this fruit today. It is bad. My mother will not buy it again. She will make dinner for us now. Because of my mother I don't know hunger, thirst and dirt}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:My friend will not come home today. He will stay at the hotel. Will he be tired? Maybe(balki), but I don't know. I will not wait for him this night}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We will not open the box. It is my present. My sister will not see it. Will she ask about it? Probably, she will not. My parents will please me today}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The big wind will not stop today. It will be cold. Will the people stay home? My parents will not open the windows}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Talk about Money[/center]\nChild: I will not forget this deficit.\nParent: That is good. We will help you think about it.\nChild: Will I make a bad choice?\nParent: No, we will teach you good logic. You will not make a bad choice."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 25,
    "text1":
        "{r:It may snow this winter and I might buy a new coat. My sister might prefer staying at home. She may not enjoy the cold weather. But my parents might go on a trip}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:I may try new food today. My friend might come with me. People may not like this food. My parents might order food for the party at home. Restaurant is just next to our house and they have fish now}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I may need repetition to understand this word. My teacher might explain it again. Because repetition is a good way to absorb knowledge completely(to'liq)}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:She might sing a song. I may become a singer. They may not like the singer. My parents usually say 'You will not be a good singer.'. This is a wrong explanation to a child}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]About Being Independent[/center]\nChild: I may depend on your help to finish this work.\nBrother: I might also depend on others for my work.\nChild: Yes, and they may depend on the weather for their trip.\nBrother: That is true. Everybody depends on something. Our parents might teach us to be independent."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 26,
    "text1":
        "{r:My grandfather is a very old person. He can talk about politics. I think politics is very interesting. I can learn much from him every day. He can teach me about the country. I always like to listen to him. We can have time together. He can tell me about old times}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:I have a new pencil. I can write my name with it. My sister has a pencil too. She can write a long letter. We can use these pencils for our homework. Is this the correct pencil for this paper? I can make a clean work with it. My parents can see my good work}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I need to buy a ticket for the train. I can go to the station today. But I can ask my father for help. He can buy the ticket. My friend can come with me to the station. We can find the ticket. I can't wait for a very long time. My parents can help me know the correct time to go}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My brother likes big cars. He says he can buy a luxurious car one day. He can also live in a big house. I think he can work very hard for this. Our parents live in a comfortable house. They always say that an easy life can make you happy but not strong(kuchli). We can learn much from them. My brother can also learn this}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Family Dinner[/center]\nChild: Mother, can I visit my grandfather this weekend?\nMother: Yes, you can! Your grandmother can make your favorite dinner. She is a great woman.\nChild: I know! I can't wait to see them. Can our family come for dinner?\nMother: Yes. We can have a big family dinner. We can eat apples too!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 27,
    "text1":
        "{r:Can you help me with this box too, or should I ask a friend? My brother can help me now. He knows about many things. I can’t open it alone. My parents can help us find the way to open the box}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Can you speak quietly, or is it too noisy here? My friend can read a book in a quiet room. They can’t do good work when it’s loud. My parents can close the door to stop the noise}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Can I borrow your pencil for a minute, or do you need it? My sister can lend me a pen. She has many of them. They can’t find their own things now. My parents can buy them new pencils soon}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Can you walk on the sandy beach, or is it too bad? My sister can build a small house in the sand. They can’t find a good beach everywhere. My parents can enjoy the beach with us}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Chess Game[/center]\nChild: Can you play chess with me, Father, or do you prefer other games?\nFather: I can play chess, my child. Your grandfather could play chess very well in the past.\nChild: That's interesting! I can’t win at chess yet. Can you teach me how to play better?\nFather: Yes, I can teach you. We can play chess every evening. You can learn fast."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 28,
    "text1":
        "{r:I must drink water every day. It is necessary for life. My glass must be full. I must not feel thirsty. My parents always say I must drink enough water. It is a good thing for every person. I can be fine}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:You must not touch that old machine. It is not safe. It can cause a bad noise. You must also not go near the lights in the room. They must be safe. You must stay inside the house tonight. It is not good to be outside with nobody at night}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I must go home immediately. It is necessary now. My father needs my help. This is very useful work. I must not be late. My parents will ask about my movement. I must do everything}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My friend is sad. I must help him. I must not say bad words. I must not make him feel bad. There must be no opposition from me. We must be good friends always}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Being Patient[/center]\nStudent: Teacher, I must know my test results now.\nTeacher: You must be patient, my child. You must wait for some time. The results will come.\nStudent: But I can't wait! It is difficult for me to be patient.\nTeacher: I understand. But you must not be sad. Your parents have always taught you to be patient, remember that."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 29,
    "text1":
        "{r:You should take a good umbrella with you today. It is very cloudy, and it may rain soon. My sister should stay inside the house if it starts raining hard. They should not make a party outside on a cloudy day. My parents should check the weather to know what to do}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:You should be very careful when you go over the road. My brother should take the glass things in a careful way. They should not be not careful with their small things. My parents should always teach us to be very careful}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:You should wear your seatbelt in the car every time you go. My friend should make her seatbelt strong(kuchli). They should not forget to use their seatbelts. My parents should tell us again to wear seatbelts for safety(xavfsizlik)}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:You should listen to your parents’ good advice. My sister should give useful advice to her friends. They should not listen to bad advice from anyone. My parents should tell their advice with us, because it is always good}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Time to Rest[/center]\nFriend A: You should take a rest after your hard work. You look tired.\nFriend B: Yes, I know. I should not work too much. My brother always says this.\nFriend A: That's right. You should rest before the big day. It is necessary.\nFriend B: You are correct. My parents always tell me again to rest when I am tired."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 30,
    "text1":
        "{r:I have a new obligation this week. I have to make a big choice(tanlov) about my personal life. Many people have an opinion about it. It is my own life, and I have to make the choice. It is necessary for me to think good. My parents always say I have to think about my nation and what is good for it. This is a big thing}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The owner of this small house has to make a big change. The house is old, and it is not safe. He has to fix(tuzatmoq) the roof and the walls(devorlar). It is a logical decision. He can't live there like this. He has to start this work immediately. This is his obligation. He will have a new house soon}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My brother is part of the military now. He has to wake up very early every morning. He has a big obligation to his nation. He has to do many hard things. Sometimes he feels nervous before a big day. But he knows it is his job. He has to be a good person for his country}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The sky is very cloudy today, and it is very windy. But we don't have to stay home. The wind is not too big, just low. It is logical to go outside for a walk. We don't have to feel sad about the weather. We can go to the park. My parents don't have to think bad things about us}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Scientist's Work[/center]\nStudent: Teacher, I have to learn about a scientist for my homework. I wonder what I have to do.\nTeacher: You actually have to know about his life. And you have to understand the meaning of his words.\nStudent: It is a gradual way, right? I don't have to finish everything quickly.\nTeacher: That is true. It is not our policy to make you nervous. A good gesture is enough. This is related to how we learn."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 31,
    "text1":
        "{r:Hello! Would you like some water? I can get it for you. It is polite to ask this. What is your preference for drinks? My mother would like to offer you a cold drink. She always thinks of others. We would like to have a good time with each other here now. We can be happy}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:My friend is thinking about his career. He would like to have a good job in the future. He thinks his choices now can have a big effect on his life later. He has a lot of good thoughts about it. Would you like to tell him about your job? He would like to learn from your experience(tajriba)}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My sister is a careful person. She wouldn't like a bad dress for the party. She is a hater of bad clothes. She wants everything to be perfect. She would like to have a new dress for the big family event(oilaviy tadbir). Would you like to help her choose? She always thinks that your opinion is good}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Our uncle would like to visit us this weekend. He is a very kind person. Our aunt would like to come with him. They would like to see our new garden. Would you like to wear your new gloves for playing outside? I'd like to play with them. They love to see us happy}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Learning New Skills[/center]\nStudent: Teacher, I'd like to learn a new skill. I am very eager to start.\nTeacher: That is good. Would you like to train your hands to work with iron? Or would you like to learn about new machines?\nStudent: I'd like to train with iron. I think it is the right thing for me.\nTeacher: Perfect! You have a good thought for your future. We can start next week."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 32,
    "text1":
        "{r:If it is cloudy today, I will take my red umbrella. It is a very useful thing. If my sister knows the weather is bad, she will stay inside the house. She thinks the cold weather can be dangerous. If we make a decision to go for a meal outside, we should not do it on a cloudy day. My parents will be happy if we keep the house clean}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:If my mother cooks a meal, it is always delicious. She has a wonderful skill. If I smell the food, I feel happy. But if the food has a bad smell, I would not like to taste it. If it is horrible, I will not eat it. My mother can cook a delicious soup from fresh plants(o'simliklar) for dinner}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:If you want good information, you should ask the teacher. It is ideal to learn new things. If the answer is incorrect, you should find the right one. If a foreign person speaks, the sound may be different. If you want to understand modern ideas, you must read new books. A book is a suitable place for information}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:If you see a sharp metal thing, you must be careful. It can be dangerous. If a child touches a sharp thing, it can hurt them. You should always tell them it is not safe. If the old brown car is on the road, it can be dangerous for people to walk near it. If you drive a car, you must be very careful}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Perfect Day[/center]\nMother: If the sun is warm, we can go to the beach. That would be ideal.\nChild: Yes! If the water is fresh and the sound of the water movement is good, it will be perfect!\nMother: That's right. If the smell of the sea is clean, we will be very happy. We should always find good places.\nChild: If everything is correct, this day will be a wonderful time to think about."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 33,
    "text1":
        "{r:I always eat my dinner slowly. It is good for my health. My parents say I should eat well. Sometimes I eat too quickly, and then I feel bad. I must take care of my body(tana) every day. It is important to live well. My family always cares for my health}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The dog suddenly ran into the room. It was a big noise. My sister shouted loudly. She felt bad. She did not want to quit her game. The dog behaved badly. We must teach the dog to behave(o'zini tutmoq) well. We must make sure it does not do this again}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The old man walks slowly and carefully. He carries a heavy bag. He does not want to fall. He thinks about everything easily. He is an intelligent person. He likes to work with green plants(o'simliklar). He always takes care of them. He does his work well and quietly}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My father always talks about innovation. He says we must find new ways to do things. My mother is pregnant now. We must take good care of her health. She can inherit good health from her mother. We have a good understanding of what she needs. We don't want her to have any illness. We are all very happy about this new life}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Doing Homework[/center]\nStudent: I want to do my homework quickly today.\nTeacher: You should do it carefully first. Doing things quickly sometimes means doing them badly.\nStudent: I want to understand everything well.\nTeacher: That is good. You can learn easily. Think slowly to understand well.\nStudent: I will try to do it well. I will not shout if it is difficult."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 34,
    "text1":
        "{r:There is a clean, white table in our kitchen. On the table, there is a small amount of salt. There are also many green growing things behind the table. There is a lot of good food in the kitchen. There is always hope for a delicious meal when my mother cooks. There are new ideas for food every day}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:There is often an argument about the new policy in our nation. There is a big population here, and everyone has an opinion. It can seem useless to talk to everyone. There is a need to consider all ideas carefully. There are many opinions, and some can lead to bad feelings. We must find a good way}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:There is good oxygen in the air we breathe. It is very important for our health. There are many small bees near the green growing things. There is much power(elektr) from the solar light of the sun. Even on a windy day, there is still energy from the sun. There are many wonders from nature in our world}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:In the court, there is a jury. There are twelve people who have to make a decision. There is often an intensive talk about the true things. There is a wish for everyone to speak fully and in a quiet way. If someone tries to rob another person, there is a way about law. There is a need for safety and what is right in the nation. Everyone must behave safely}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Waiting in the Sun[/center]\nFriend 1: There are no good sunglasses here. I want to buy new ones.\nFriend 2: Yes, there is nowhere to buy them right now. We have to wait in a patient way.\nFriend 1: It is hard to wait in a patient way. There is always a lot to do.\nFriend 2: True. But there is a good opinion about waiting. It helps us become big."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 35,
    "text1":
        "{r:Last night, there was a robbery near the big bank. There was a small, brown wallet taken from a person. There was a loud yell from the street. The police came quickly. There were many people who saw the event. It was a serious legal problem. There was much noise, but the police worked well to make it safe again}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Yesterday, there was a very tasty meal for dinner. My mother cooked it for the family. There were many vegetables in the soup, like onion and potato. All the food had a good smell and taste. There was also a delicious bread. Everyone said there was nothing bad about the meal. It was an actual wonderful meal for all of us}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:In the big company, there was a very strong boss. He was the leader for many years. There was a good relation between the boss and his workers. Personally, I think there was no weak person in his group. Everyone worked well. There were many intelligent people. There was never an argument. He was a very good leader}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Early in the morning, there was a thick fog outside. It was hard to see much. There was a long queue of people at the corner of the street. Everyone was waiting in patiently. There was a small paper in my hand. I had to get a signature for them. There were many people in the queue, and they moved slowly}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Old Town[/center]\nGrandfather: When I was a boy, there was a small shop at this corner. There was a kind owner there.\nChild: Really? Was there a big tree also? I think there is a big tree here now.\nGrandfather: Yes, there was. And there were many people. There was always a long queue for fresh bread."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 36,
    "text1":
        "{r:It is very important to improve your skills every day. It can seem impossible sometimes, but it is not a myth. It is good to try any new way to learn. It is always best to concentrate well. It was a good idea to put a strong light in the room to help us study. It helps us see everything better}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:It was a terrible sound from the street last night. I think it was a big accident. My friend called me immediately to tell me the news. I had to go quickly, but I missed the train to the city. I do not want to repeat that bad experience. I promise to be more careful next time. It is not good to miss important things}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The number of people in the city can increase every year. It is dependent on many factors. The number of trees can decrease if we are not careful. It is important to watch the flow of water in the river. If there is a lot of rain, it will flow quickly. It is good to have honey, but it is not always easy to get it. It is sweet and delicious}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:It is always good to act kindly to others. It is an important act of a good person. Sometimes, people do not listen, but it is good to insist on what is right. We should employ more people at our company. Ideally, it would be good to give jobs to everyone who needs one. It helps the nation improve its life. It is not an impossible dream}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The New Cookie[/center]\nFriend A: This is a new cookie. Would you like to try it?\nFriend B: Yes! It smells delicious. It is big and round. I will eat it slowly to taste it well.\nFriend A: It is a special cookie. It is made with honey.\nFriend B: Wow! It is perfect. I insist on having another one later."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 37,
    "text1":
        "{r:Who saw anything strange last night in the street? The police want to know. Who spoke to the new person? They need information. Who is the leader of our national group? We want to follow him well. Who made this lovely material? It is perfect for a new dress. Who can translate this old book for me? It seems very important}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Who did you see at the party yesterday? I hope you saw many friends. Who did your brother call immediately? Was it his boss? Who did she give that big cookie to? It was very tasty. Who did you tell about the missing wallet? It is important to tell the police. Who did they choose to lead the work? He is very intelligent}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Who was sick last week? I hope they feel better now. Who is a considerate person in your family? It is good to have such a relative. Who helped you find the missing cheese? It is a food I really love. Who did the company employ recently? We need more workers. Who did you ask about the new national policy? Was it the leader?}",
    "text4":
        "{r:Who can legally buy this land? It is a big question. Who has a good fortune in this life? Seemingly, many people feel happy. Who did you meet yesterday? Was it anybody from our old school? Who did the owner employ to work in his shop? He always wants good people. Who wants to try anything new? It is always good to learn}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Missing Book[/center]\nBrother: Who took my favorite book? It is missing now.\nSister: Who did you see near your room this morning? Maybe it was a small child.\nBrother: I didn't see anybody. But who would want my old book?\nSister: Hopefully, we can find it. Who helps us find missing things in this house?"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 38,
    "text1":
        "{r:My friend is marrying soon. Who is she planning to talk to about her wedding dress? She always wants the best advice. There is a problem, and I am worried. We want to help her and we need to take action immediately. My uncle said he heard a strange sound. It seemed very loud. Who did the news come from this morning? I don't know but everyone wants to respond quickly to good news. This situation needs attention}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:There is a new building in the city center. What is it like? Is it modern? I hear it is very tall. The moon rose early last night. What was it like? Was it big and bright? It can seem very beautiful. The small child asked about his new toy. What is it like? Does it weigh much? Is it heavy or light? He wants to play with any new thing. It was left on the table}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I met the new boss yesterday. What is he like? Is he a good leader? I hope he shows respect to all his workers. What were the new members(a'zo) of the group like? Did they take good action? It is important to attract attention with positive work. What are the children like in the new school? Do they pay attention in class? We want them to learn well. We need good teachers for them to become big and intelligent}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:There is a new system for the work. What is it like? Is it a big improvement? We hope it can satisfy everyone. The new book recommends a better way to distribute goods. What is the book like? Is it easy to understand? I hope it is. The weather is good today. What is it like outside now? Is the rain falling lightly? Yes it is. We hope it is a beautiful day for everyone}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A New Experience[/center]\nPerson A: I went to a new restaurant yesterday. What was it like?\nPerson B: Oh, really? What was the food like? Was it tasty?\nPerson A: Yes, it was delicious. But it was very busy. Who did you go with?\nPerson B: I didn't go. But my cousin went. What was he thinking about when he chose that place?\nPerson A: He wants to try new places. It's a way to attract attention to his food website."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 39,
    "text1":
        "{r:What size is your new laptop? Is it big or small? What type of work do you do on it? It seems very useful. What kind of sweater do you like to wear in cold weather? What colour is your favourite one? What kind of problems do newcomers face when they are homesick? It's important to understand their feelings. What is the most important thing for a good family? What kind of life do you want to have?}",
    "text2":
        "{r:There were two teams in the game. Which opponent was stronger? Which team played better? The fans started to complain loudly when their team lost. Which source of information did you use to know this? Some people like to argue about the score. Which kind of leadership style do you think is best for a big group? Which leader attracts the most attention? Which decision was the most difficult for the team?}",
    "text3":
        "{r:How high is the new building? It looks very tall from here. How fast do trees grow in this area? How old must a person be to join this brotherhood? How attentive are the students in the class today? It is important for them to learn well. How often does your family celebrate important events? How long have you lived in this city? How much money do you need for your future plans?}",
    "text4":
        "{r:What kind of architecture do you like? Do you prefer old buildings or modern ones? Which drawing is your favourite from this book? It seems very beautiful. How difficult is it to become a good translator? What kind of person can do it well? How often do you work without your laptop? Is it hard to be without it? What is the most important thing for good health? What kind of problems can we solve together?}",
    "text5":
        "[center]Looking to the Future[/center]\nFriend A: What do you want to do after school? What kind of job are you looking for?\nFriend B: I want a job where I can grow. How much money do you think is enough for a good life?\nFriend A: It's difficult to say. How long do you plan to study? Which university is best for you?\nFriend B: I'm not sure. But I want to be an honest person. What kind of person are you? Are you funny or sad often?\nFriend A: I try to be funny and honest. What kind of friend do you need without any problems?"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 40,
    "text1":
        "{r:Do you know where the smoke is coming from? It smells strong. I don't know what the weight of that box is. Can you tell me how much it contains? I want to apologize to my friend, but I don't know why he is angry. What is his biggest concern right now? Can you tell me what time the next lesson starts? I don't want to be late. It is important to learn well}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Do you know how big an elephant is? They are truly huge animals. I don't know how long it takes for a new reader to finish a big book. Do you know where the lively party happened last night? It was very loud. Can you tell me if the weather will be rainy tomorrow? I need to plan. We don't remember what the monthly meeting was about. Why did they go home early? This is a question we need to answer}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Do you know if he will come to the special occasion? I hope he does. Can you tell me whether it's a typical problem for new students?. Do you realize if this box can contain all the books? We need more space. I don't remember if that book consists of many chapters. It seems very long}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Do you know why some people behave in a selfish way? It's often hard to understand their feeling. I don't know what a happy life consists of exactly. Can you tell me where the best place to buy a new laptop is? I want to know how much it costs. Do you know if your friend will apologize for his bad actions? It is important to solve problems. I don't remember when the next monthly report will come. It should be soon}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]About Our Lesson[/center]\nStudent: Teacher, do you know what time our next lesson starts?\nTeacher: I don't know exactly. But do you know if you finished the last lesson's reading?\nStudent: I finished it. But I don't know why that reader felt so sad. Was it because he was selfish?\nTeacher: I cannot tell you exactly why he felt that way. But do you know if he will apologize for his bad behaviour?\nStudent: I hope so. It's a difficult lesson for him to learn."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 41,
    "text1":
        "{r:The manager said that the meeting would be held weekly. He told me that he often played the piano in the evenings. Fortunately, she said that she could come to the stadium to watch the game. My friend told me that he read the news repeatedly every morning. I heard a reporter say that the recent event was very important for the city's future}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The company leader told us that there would be a delay in the new project. He said that the situation looked suspicious to many people. The boss told me that we had to face the problems directly and quickly. A financial expert said that the profit would increase significantly this month. She said that she felt confident about the company's future and its growth}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My travel agent said that the bus fare for the trip was too high. She told me that I should reserve my seat early to avoid any trouble. He said that the new train line would connect the two big cities easily and quickly. The teacher told the students that they should mark their answers carefully on the test. She said that following all the rules was always important for success}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:He told me that he felt confident about the exam results and expected a good score. My sister said that she had seen a suspicious person near our house recently. She told me that she would report it directly to the police immediately. 'Fortunately, our team made a good profit last quarter, which was an improvement' said the speaker. He said that we should listen to his speech very carefully. He told us that there was no possibility for any delay in our work}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]News and Plans[/center]\nPerson A: Did Mary say anything about the party?\nPerson B: Yes, she said that she was confident it would be fun. She told me that she had reserved a large space.\nPerson A: What did the reporter say about the recent news?\nPerson B: He said that there was a delay in the report. He told me that the information was still being collected following some issues.\nPerson A: That's a concern. Did he say if there would be any profit from this plan?\nPerson B: He only said that it was too early to tell, but he seemed hopeful."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 42,
    "text1":
        "{r:I enjoy living in the city, but I wanted to experience something new. I decided to go to the sea. I planned to get a ship to another country. My friend said, 'I would like to come with you.' We decided to discuss the trip. My friend likes traveling and continued to talk about all the places we could go. We hoped to find the best place to go}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:We talked about everything. My friend suggested going to the north, but I refused to go there. I wanted to travel to the south. He seemed surprised by my behavior. He said, 'I don't mind changing our plan. I just want to have a good time with you.' The situation was a little concerning for me, but I didn't want to get upset. We continued our talk and found a good plan together}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We wanted to inform our parents about our trip directly. My brother said he would help. He knew the easiest way. I said I would report our plan to our mother. He promised to inform our father. We started to get ready for our trip. We began to collect the things we would need. We wanted to hide our plans from some of our other friends to surprise them later}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:On the ship, we ate a wonderful dish. The temperature was fine. I didn't experience any problems with my health. We did not have any kind of disease. I enjoyed watching the fish in the sea. I promised to get a new dish recipe for my mother. I like to swim in the sea, so I planned to swim every day. I began to feel very happy about our trip}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Happy Journey[/center]\nFriend: How was the trip? Was the weather good?\nMe: It was wonderful! My favorite experience was swimming in the sea. The ship was very good, and we ate a delicious dish every night.\nFriend: Did you find any problems?\nMe: No. The temperature was perfect. I was worried, because I would hate to get a strange disease.\nFriend: Would you mind helping me to collect some books for school tomorrow?\nMe: Of course not! I would like to help. We can discuss it after I finish my food."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 43,
    "text1":
        "{r:The company manager wants us to start a big new project this year. They intend the team to finish all the necessary work quickly. I didn't expect them to give me so much important work in the beginning. Sometimes, I want my friend to help me carry all these project papers – they are very heavy! The manager would like everyone to feel confident about our goals. He expects us to work together closely to make this a success}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Our team leader always tries to encourage us to share new ideas during meetings. He advised me to speak directly about any complaint I had. We told him not to force anyone to work extra hours if they didn't want to. He asked us to persuade the new follower to join our discussion group. Some members(a'zo) used to beg him to change some decisions, but he always told them to follow the team's main recommendation}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The recent project delay made everyone feel worried, but it also made us think more deeply. The pressure made us work very hard outside of planned hours. The need for new solutions made the workers invent new ways. We hoped that our efforts would make the clients feel great satisfaction. We also had to make sure the new members use the new methods correctly. A problem can make people grow and learn quickly}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:After the main difficulties, the manager decided to let everyone have a short break. This decision would enable the team to come back with more energy. We also decided to let a few experienced members lead small groups. Our goal is to let every follower help fully with the growth of the company. We won't let any small problem stop our progress now. Let's discuss the next steps together in the following meeting}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Project Success[/center]\nLeader: I wanted to tell you personally that I'm pleased with our project's success. What made you work so hard?\nMember: Thank you! I think knowing you expect us to give our best really encouraged everyone. Also, you let us invent new solutions.\nLeader: I'm glad. Did anyone complain about the long hours, or did the pressure make them perform better?\nMember: At first, some found it difficult, but you advised us to stay positive. And the promise of seeing growth made us continue.\nLeader: That's good. We must enable the team to always find this level of satisfaction in their work."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 44,
    "text1":
        "{r:The new student went to the office to get his map. He needed it to find the correct direction to his class. He didn't have much time to look around. He also went to the university shop to buy some books. He needed some money to pay a bill for his course. He hopes to develop his skills quickly this year}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:A group of workers went to the big city for a new project. They also went for a meeting with the main speaker. They needed a good plan for their work. They went to the restaurant for a meal after their discussions. There was some doubt about the plan, but they all began to agree it would be profitable. They worked hard for the success of the company, avoiding any trouble}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Please wait for me after the class. I need to ask the speaker a question. I am waiting to go to the library now. Are you waiting for the bus? We are all waiting to see the first results of the experiment. The doctor told me to wait for an hour before moving my arm. She is able to wait patiently}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I can't go inside the building yet. I'm waiting for the main door to open. The nurse was waiting for the doctor to check the patient. He was worried the patient might bleed from his arm. They gave him a drug to help him. We are waiting for the ambulance to arrive quickly. It's usual for such things to happen in big hospitals. We just need to develop a better system}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]First Day at Work[/center]\nManager: Welcome! I'm here to show you your desk and the office Space. Please don't doubt that you are able to learn quickly.\nEmployee: Thank you! I'm ready to start. I came early to prepare. I'm waiting for my laptop to connect to the network.\nManager: Ah, yes. The IT team is waiting to help. We expect you to have good confidence in this job. We want you to enjoy your work for the company's growth.\nEmployee: I will! I'm ready to apply my skills. I'm also waiting for a recommendation from the finance group to begin my first task.\nManager: Good. This project is profitable, so we need everyone to work well. Let's make sure there is no trouble."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 45,
    "text1":
        "{r:What time do you plan to go to the city center? I plan to go to the city center later to buy some new clothes. We wanted to go to a concert last night, but we couldn't find tickets. After a long day, I always go home directly. My friend was very tired and wanted to go to sleep quickly. He hoped his new business would develop well. Before we leave, we need to check the map for the correct direction. We have a regular meeting to check the project bill}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Next month, my family is going on holiday to a beautiful island. Children often go on school trips to learn new things. We decided to go for a long walk after work yesterday. Do you often go for a run in the morning? The sea looks nice; let's go for a swim. We went for a drink after the meeting to discuss the new project. Everyone will agree that this is a profitable idea. There is no doubt it will avoid future trouble. The workers have gone on strike for a second time because of the low pay. They are asking for a cruise on the company boat as a reward}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Are you going shopping this afternoon? I need to buy some food and new clothes. It's a nice day; let's go swimming in the lake. Rachel has a small boat and she often goes sailing on the sea. Before breakfast this morning, I went jogging for an hour. It is important to be strong and able to do physical activity. Our team has first place in the competition. The main speaker will talk about games}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:He came inside the house quickly because it started to rain. Sometimes when people are very sick, they need a drug from the doctor. If someone has an injury, they might bleed. In an emergency, we must call an ambulance quickly. We planned to go to the hospital to see a friend. We had to go for a short walk to find help. The accident caused a lot of trouble and delay for everyone. There was a suspicion that someone tried to deny what happened. His refusal to tell the truth made things more difficult. We didn't doubt that they would develop a solution}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Weekend Plans and Trust[/center]\nPerson A: Are you going to the new stadium this weekend?\nPerson B: No, I don't think so. I usually go for a run on Saturday morning. And I might go shopping in the afternoon.\nPerson A: Oh. I hoped you would go on a trip with us. We are going to the sea to experience sailing on my boat.\nPerson B: I can't this time. I have a lot of work on my desk. My confidence in finishing everything is a bit low. I need to develop a new plan. I have a suggestion for a second time we can meet.\nPerson A: I see. Let's go for a drink after work one day soon. I have great trust in your judgment. That's a good tradition. I have a high expectation for your persuasion skills.\nPerson B: I will be respectful of your time."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 46,
    "text1":
        "{r:Did you get my message from your neighbor yesterday? I sent it. My friend needs to get a new job soon; it's very difficult now. Where did you get that nice book? I want to get one too. Can you please get me a letter from the table? It's for my boss. I hope to get an answer quickly}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:If you don't eat, you get hungry quickly. Drink your coffee. It's getting cold here. I'm sorry your mother is ill. I hope she gets better soon. My brother and his partner are getting married next month. I got up and got dressed quickly this morning. We went for a walk in the forest and got lost. It was a mistake to go there without a map. I feel very forgetful these days; it can bother me sometimes. I hope I don't get stupid}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I get to work before 8:30 regularly. We left London at 10 o'clock and got to Manchester at 12:45. How did you get here? By bus? What time did you get home last night? A local group of artists will appear at the main theater. We hope many people recognize their hard work. The development of this new area is changing the city greatly}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Kate got in the car and drove away. A car stopped and a man got out. We got on the bus outside the hotel and got off in Church Street. It was a cold night, so I quickly got into my warm bed with my pillow. The door was shut, but she tried to open it forcefully. She needed to get inside. She will succeed in opening it, I have no doubt}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day of Travel[/center]\nTom: Did you get my message about our trip? The third meeting is tomorrow.\nAnn: Yes, I got it. I hope we don't get lost this time! I need to get to the station early to get on the train.\nTom: Don't worry. I will help. But after the long journey, you might get tired. What time do you expect to get home?\nAnn: I hope to get home before night. I will get dressed quickly for dinner if we arrive before seven o'clock. Did you get a good bill for our hotel?\nTom: Yes, I did. I was able to get a good price. I also need to get a special drug for my father. After that, I will get in the car and get him."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 47,
    "text1":
        "{r:Every morning, my neighbor Jane does a lot of things. She does the cooking for her family, and then she does the washing. Her job is not boring; she does something new every day. She helps people. When she is not working, she does her exercises regularly. What are you doing this evening? I am doing my best to finish my work quickly today}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:After doing her daily tasks, Jane likes to make things. Making clothes is her favorite hobby. She makes dresses and jackets for children. She also makes small toys. She believes in doing things well to create a good example for others. She says the engine of her old sewing machine helps her make wonderful things. She often makes a phone call to her friends to share her ideas}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Next week, Jane is doing a driving test. She has also just done a training course for her job. Sometimes her children do their homework in the same room while she does housework. She especially hates doing the ironing. Could you do her a favour and help her do the shopping this weekend? She always tries to do her best, even when things are difficult}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Yesterday, Jane made a big mistake with her schedule. She made an appointment for the wrong time, which caused some confusion. She also made a lot of noise trying to fix an old clock, and it made her feel strange. She usually makes her bed every morning, but yesterday she forgot to do it. She hopes this is not a sign of the worst times for her income. She knows she needs to work hard to succeed}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day with Jane[/center]\nFriend: Hi Jane! What are you doing today? Are you making anything new?\nJane: Hello! Yes, I’m doing a lot. I’m making a new toy, and I need to do some housework. It’s always busy!\nFriend: I have sympathy for you. Doing housework can be difficult. Did you make that beautiful dress you're wearing?\nJane: Yes, I did! I made it last month. I try to make fair clothes for everyone. Do you have any suggestions for my next project?\nFriend: Hmm. Perhaps you could make a list of your ideas. We can have a discussion later. You are always so caring and healthy; it’s a good example to all of us. You will not be a loser."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 48,
    "text1":
        "{r:I work with a new team. They are very successful. She is a promising actress; I often see her on TV. He is also an actor, and I think he has great talent. When I speak to him, he always gives me good advice. Sometimes they want to hear my ideas, and I give them strong support. We all know each other well now, and we expect to create something big together}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:I have a good book here about art. You can have it after I finish it. I don't want these old clothes. You can take them if you like them. Do you want some coffee? I can make it for you. This table is too small. I cannot put all these things on it. My friend doesn't like parties; she never goes to them because they cause too much noise}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:This new project is difficult, but I believe in our team. This letter isn't for me, it's for him. Who is that woman? Why are you looking at her? We are going to the cinema this evening. Do you want to come with us? Sue and Kevin are going to the concert. Do you want to go with them? There is no blame for this small mistake. With good consideration and intelligence, we will succeed}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My small baby likes to play. He tries to get everything. Please give that toy to him. It is his favorite. This old pillow is not comfortable; please throw it away. My friend has a bad cough and flu. I will give him a drug to help him get better. I saw a small tiger in my dream last night. It had a big head. The dream was strange, but I will not let it bother me}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Team Project[/center]\nPerson A: I need to discuss the project details. Do you have time for me?\nPerson B: Yes, I do. Tell me about it. We can work on it together. I trust your judgment.\nPerson A: I'm worried about a part of the engine. It's making a strange noise. We need to fix it.\nPerson B: I hear you. We have a good team. Let's ask the General for his advice. He has great intelligence. He usually gives us good suggestions.\nPerson A: That's a good idea. I will ask him. I hope he can give us some support. I believe we can make this project successful if we work strongly."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 49,
    "text1":
        "{r:I like my new job. It is challenging. We all enjoy our work very much. You can see your progress every day. My friend, Tom, likes his car; he always cleans it. Sarah enjoys her garden; she spends a lot of time there. The team likes their project; they are working hard on its development. Every person gives their best ability to the group}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Look at my hands; they are cold. His mother is visiting him this week. Our house is next to the big park. Your best friend is coming to the party tonight. Her new car is very fast, and her son loves to ride in it. Their room is always clean. And their daughter helps them with housework. I admire their family and their strong traditions}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The old tree in our garden is very beautiful. Its leaves turn red every autumn. It's a very old tree, and it's famous in our local area. My city is proud of its history. It's a nice place to live. It's easy to get around because its roads are in good condition. It's important to understand the difference between its and it's when you write}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:John's employment originally started last year. He got his first salary last month. He always puts his important papers in his desk drawer. One day, he heard a strange noise. It was a mouse trying to get into his house, perhaps caught in a trap near its edge. He felt a cough in his throat and gave a small apology for making a noise. His immediate response was to get a kettle of water to make tea}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Family Day[/center]\nFather: What are your plans for today, my daughter?\nDaughter: I will play with my toy. It's my favorite. And then I will do my homework.\nFather: That's good. Your brother has his own work too. He is working on his new painting. His ability to create is great.\nMother: And I'm doing my housework. My kitchen is not very clean, but its floor is. I hope our son and daughter will help me. I need their support today.\nSon: Yes, Mother! We will help you. We will do our best. I admire your caring nature. Its influence on us is important."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 50,
    "text1":
        "{r:My hands are cold today. Is this your book? I think it is yours, not mine. Ann gave me her umbrella when it started to rain. I didn’t have one, so she gave me hers. This is their problem, not our problem. It is not ours. We went in our car, and they went in theirs. Whose turn is it to get coffee? I think it's his}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Whose money is this on the table? It's mine, of course. Whose shoes are these under the desk? They are John's. Whose camera is this? Is it his or hers? It’s his. Whose recipe is this for the big cake? It looks very old. Whose kettle is this that is still hot? Perhaps it's yours. It's important to know whose belongings are whose to avoid any confusion}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I went out to meet a friend of mine yesterday. She was with a friend of hers. Are those people friends of yours? They look familiar. They are very attractive and seem happy. We talked about a strange event that happened locally. The basic idea of the story did not originate in our town; it was a translation from an old book. Its words were very pure and beautiful}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:This small statue is made of pure gold and stone. Its value is very high. Whose is it? We saw a mouse running on the edge of the room. It tried to get into a trap. Its little head moved quickly. We heard a new report about a hidden treasure. The report said we would need to dive into the sea to find it. Some paper was wet and started to stick to the floor. It was an uncomfortable situation to deal with, like paying a new tax}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Mysterious Finding[/center]\nPerson A: Whose book is this? It was on my chair.\nPerson B: Hmm, it's not mine. Is it hers, perhaps? She was sitting there earlier.\nPerson A: No, it's not hers. Her book has a different cover. Is it yours? Or maybe it's his, that friend of yours who visits regularly?\nPerson B: Of course, it's his! I recognize its strange mark on the back. He likes to mark his books. And whose candle is this on the table? It's almost new.\nPerson A: That's ours! We put it there for the special evening event. It's good that we know whose things are whose."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 51,
    "text1":
        "{r:I saw my colleague, Mark, recently. He was trying to fix a problem with his new invention. I wanted to help him, but he seemed frustrated. His face showed a lot of effort. I know his work is important to him. I always try to impress him with my own progress. It is important to me that we work together to make a strong connection}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:My sister, Sarah, also works with us. She has her own project. We like her ideas very much. We try to give her our full support. Have you seen her designs? They are very creative. The team believes in their consistency. They are all experienced engineers, and their work is always excellent. They often discuss their next steps with each other}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our team is working on a new application for a survey. It is a big project. We believe in its success. We decided to raise the height of the model we are building. This allows us to determine its full ability. It is our hope that this invention will help many people. We will present it to our boss soon. This project is ours, and we are proud of it}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Firstly, a friend of mine came to visit the office. He saw the mess on my desk. I owed him an apology for it. He said, ‘You must fix this mess around your bench!’ It was his way to help me set things right. Sometimes, it feels like fighting an enemy, but it's just my own lack of organization. His advice is always good, and I listen to him carefully}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Project's Journey[/center]\nPerson A: How is your project going, Mark? I saw your colleague helping you recently.\nMark: It's going well, thank you. He always helps me fix problems. His experience is very valuable to us.\nPerson A: That's great! Your invention has a lot of potential. I hear its application is quite complex. Is it yours or the team's?\nMark: It's ours. We all work on it. My work, his work, her work – they all come together. We try to impress ourselves and our boss with its consistency.\nPerson A: Excellent! I admire your team. I hope you can raise its height and show its full ability. You don't owe anyone an apology for your hard work!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 52,
    "text1":
        "{r:A young soldier looked at himself in the mirror. He saw a tired face. He hoped he would not burn himself with the hot water. He used a clean towel to dry himself. He told himself to be strong for the difficult journey ahead. Sometimes, he spoke to himself to express his thoughts. He felt ashamed if he ever doubted himself. He wanted to do his duty}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Secondly, the soldier’s army was preparing for a long voyage across the river. The General told them, ‘You must protect yourselves and each other. We will carry our own plates and reward ourselves with a good meal after we succeed.’ They decided to work together to load the boat. They knew they had to be careful not to hurt themselves during the hard work. Generally, they were a strong and unified group}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:During the voyage, one soldier had to go by himself to find more supplies at a small store near the river. He walked alone, thinking about his family. He often found himself talking to himself when he was by himself in the quiet nature. He remembered a denial from someone, and felt ashamed about it. He hoped to return quickly to his friends and share the supplies, without feeling like a loser}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:In the night, the army felt a sudden attack. The soldiers looked at each other, ready to fight. They did not look at themselves, but at the enemy in front of them. They had to defend themselves strongly. There was an accusation of a past mistake, but they put it aside. Their leader told them not to blame themselves for the trouble, but to act together for their safety. They fought hard for each other}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Return from the Voyage[/center]\nCaptain: Welcome back, soldiers! You have returned from a long voyage. How do you all feel?\nSoldier 1: We are tired, Captain, but we enjoyed ourselves when we saw our homes again. We supported each other every day.\nSoldier 2: Yes, we are proud of ourselves. We did not let the difficult conditions make us tired. We made sure to look after ourselves.\nCaptain: Excellent! This is a great reward. Your appearance and recognition are strong. There is no need for any denial or accusation. I want to give you all my congratulation. You expressed great courage.\nSoldier 1: Thank you, Captain. We feel good about ourselves. We will generally do our best for the army."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 53,
    "text1":
        "{r:Recently, I visited my nephew’s house in a small village. It’s a quiet place. My sister’s car was already there. We talked about my brother’s new job. The manager’s office in his company is very modern. My nephew’s camera was on the table. It was a nice camera. I stayed at my sister’s house, not my mother’s, that night}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Inside the house, my mother’s favorite painting was on the wall. Mary’s room was always clean, unlike mine. Whose book is this on the top of the shelf? Perhaps it’s a friend’s book. My friend’s hair is longer than Ann’s. I remember when my parents’ room was full of old pictures. A friend of mine came to Paul’s house yesterday, so we had a big discussion}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The name of this village is Green Hills. The roof of the main building is very old. We talked about the cause of the problem about the river. We didn’t see the beginning of the local festival. There was a small tear on the last page of the village history book. The main topic of our discussion was the environment. The edge of the forest was very thin, which was a strange part of the view}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:In the village, there was a creative project on a wall. It was the work of a talented artist. We talked about the best part of the design. The artist’s idea was to mix many colors.Its color began to look strange. The thin wood began to tear a little from the strong wind. This project needed our full supportive help}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Village Art and Life[/center]\nSarah: This neighborhood is so peaceful! Whose creative art is this on the big building?\nTom: That's the work of a friend of mine. She's a talented artist from this village. Her ideas always impress me.\nSarah: I admire her work! The colors mix well. What's the main topic of her new project?\nTom: It's about community exchange. She wants people to be supportive of each other. She believes it's the best part of art.\nSarah: I agree. Its message is powerful. I bet that it will be very successful. This village has great creative energy!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 54,
    "text1":
        "{r:It was a messy part of the garden, and autumn was coming. I needed a tool to fix that. I had a strong determination to do it by myself. Can I ask you a question? Do you have a hammer? I need a good one to help me. I want people to be impressed by my beautiful garden}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:I started to lay new stones for a path. It was a frustrating job at first, but I kept my determination. I found a golden carrot in the soil, which gave me a good feeling. I thought, 'This is a nice reward!' Sometimes I had to kneel to get a closer look at the work. I hoped the rain wouldn't affect my progress too much. It was a simple task, but it took a lot of effort}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I needed to make a deal for some new accommodation for my trip. It had to be a private room. I saw a house with a very attractive garden. I spoke to a man who owned it. He was a kind person, and I had a lot of admiration for his work. He told me, 'This is a fair price, and it's not an illegal deal.' He made a strong impression on me with his honesty}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:A friend of mine had a small accident. He got a cut, and there was some blood. It was a moment of concern, and I quickly offered to help him. I called for an ambulance. It was a serious situation, but he had a strong determination to stay calm. He was an example of courage. I believe a good friend always offers help when you need it most. This event had a strong effect on me}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Private Deal[/center]\nFriend: I hear you found a new accommodation. Was it a good deal?\nYou: Yes, it was a fair price. I made a deal with an owner. I have a lot of admiration for his direct way of doing business.\nFriend: That’s great! Was it easy to find?\nYou: Not at first. It was a bit frustrating. But I had a clear determination. I saw a duck in his garden and felt a strange impression.\nFriend: A duck? That's funny."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 55,
    "text1":
        "{r:I have a car, and it's a very old car, but it runs well. There are many cars in the city, but my dream is to escape them. I want to visit an island this summer. I think it will be a wonderful experience. I can already taste a sweet grape in my mind as I plan. I have two books ready for the journey, and I’ve even bought a new pen to write notes}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:To get ready for my trip, I bought some new items. I need a piece of soap for the bathroom and some shampoo. I also picked a new perfume bottle; I like to have a fresh smell. Money isn't everything, but I need some money for the journey. There isn’t much money in my wallet right now, so I will save more. Water is essential, of course, and air is everywhere}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My house is full of furniture, but I plan to take very little with me. I have a big wooden table and a comfortable chair, which are pieces of my home. I will only take a small bowl for my food and a bucket for the beach. I also need a piece of bread for the first day. It's important to pack light. I believe a piece of useful advice is to travel with a simple heart}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:This journey feels important to me. I sent an envelope with my plans to a partner of mine who will be my guide. There is a big difference between dreaming and doing. I had a sleepless night thinking about all the details. My partner’s expression was full of happiness when I told him. I hope any small problems will disappear during our adventure. The value of this experience will be great}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Summer Island Trip[/center]\nFriend: So, your trip to the island this summer is finally set? That's wonderful!\nYou: Yes! I've packed a small bucket for the beach and a new bottle of perfume. I hope my sleepless nights planning will finally disappear!\nFriend: I'm sure they will. Did you get a good guide for the island?\nYou: Yes, my partner will be my guide. He knows every part of the island. He said, 'A true guide shows the difference between the land and the sea.' I also have some grapes for our journey.\nFriend: That's excellent. What about food? Did you pack a piece of cheese?\nYou: Not yet! But I have a bowl for my food. The importance of this trip has a high value to me. It's more than just a holiday."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 56,
    "text1":
        "{r:Recently, I found a new flat. It has a white ceiling and a soft carpet. I’m going to clean the flat tomorrow. It has a big living room. There is a comfortable chair in the corner. I asked a question about the small problems with the heating. The person who answered was a helpful guide. There was a big table in the kitchen, and it needed a good cleaning}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Inside the flat, everything was clear. I opened the door to the bathroom first. The floor was clean, and the light was bright. The mirror on the wall was new. I looked up at the ceiling; it was painted a light grey color. The carpet in the bedroom felt warm under my feet. I need to buy a new towel for the bathroom. It’s important to make sure the flat is comfortable for me}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Life in the city can be busy. Sometimes, a person needs a lot of patience. There are many opinions about what is justice. Some believe a violent act is never justified. The capital of our country is always full of people. My elder brother said that an average person works many hours. In spring, the city is especially beautiful. Sometimes, I feel a pain in my stomach after eating too much. It's a common problem}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I saw a big shark at the aquarium last year. Its grey skin was strange to see. It was a powerful animal. I walked on a straight road to get to the church in the village. It was a beautiful old building. My elder sister has an insurance policy for her car. She says it’s very important. She also has a long neck, like a model. She is an average height for a woman. She gives very helpful advice}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Flat's New Life[/center]\nFriend: So, how is the new flat? Is it comfortable?\nMe: Yes, it's very nice! The carpet in the living room is so soft. And the ceiling is high. It's a very clear space. I spent an hour cleaning the bathroom yesterday.\nFriend: Good! Did you find the key to the door?\nMe: Yes, I found it! I also turned on the light. It was a simple task. My elder sister said it's important to have a good home insurance. She's always helpful.\nFriend: She gives good advice. Are you worried about anything, like a strange animal?\nMe: No, not really. I have a lot of patience. My stomach feels good. I just want to enjoy my new place. I think it's a good flat for an average person like me."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 57,
    "text1":
        "{r:What is the name of this neighborhood? My apartment is on the first floor of the building. I live near the city centre. Sometimes, I need to find the nearest grocery store. I often use the dictionary to look up words. My colleague and I live in the same street. We work for the same office. Presently, he is the best player in our team. We sometimes count the cars in the street. The capital of our country is a very busy place}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Every morning, I look at the sky. The sun is shining, and the world feels peaceful. I prefer to live in the country, not in a town. My brother is a soldier; he’s in the army. He works at the top of a big hill. My house is at the end of this long road. The table is in the middle of the room. When I drive, I always stay on the right side of the road. I believe in peace for the environment}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I love music. My sister is learning to play the piano, and I play the guitar. We listen to the radio a lot in the evening. I watch television sometimes, but not tonight. What's on television tonight? I don't know. My father believes in a strong religion. He says it gives him a good sense of purpose. He has a high degree in history. He always tells me to try my best}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:What did you have for breakfast today? Dinner is ready at six o’clock. I am not working next week. Did you have a holiday last summer? A political visitor came to our city recently. He spoke about important matters. It is a crime to commit certain acts. We believe in justice for all. He gave us valuable guidance for the future. The toilet in the old building was broken, and it needed a fix}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]City Life and Beliefs[/center]\nFriend: So, you live near the city centre. What’s the name of your street?\nMe: It’s Green Street. My apartment is on the second floor. It's the same street as my elder sister.\nFriend: Do you like living in the city or in the country?\nMe: I like both. The city has good transport, but the country has fresh air. I prefer to be where the sky is clear. What's on television tonight?\nFriend: I don't know. I was listening to the radio earlier. My father says the world needs more patience. He has a strong belief in peace. He says it gives him a good sense of guidance for the future. He has a high degree of knowledge.\nMe: I agree. What did you have for breakfast?"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 58,
    "text1":
        "{r:This morning started with some chaos. I felt sore in my neck from a bad night's sleep, and I was quite impatient to begin my day. My room was a messy sight. I saw a tiny ant walking on the wall. I looked out the window of my apartment and saw a tall skyscraper in the city. I tried to think about my work correctly. I knew a foreigner would visit soon, and I wanted to be ready}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Later, I had to experience a small problem with a pipe in my kitchen. The water was dripping. I needed a plumber to install a new pipe. I called to book an appointment with him. He was a sensible man and his answers were straightforward. He was not shy when he told me the price. He said it would be a quick fix. I hoped he would arrive soon to help me}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:While waiting, I read a book. The story was full of irony; the hero always found the truth in the most difficult places. I thought about life. An eagle flew high in the sky, a beautiful sight. It made me think about freedom. I believe it is impolite to ask for personal details. Sometimes, it is important to be silent and just observe. The world holds many lessons}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The plumber arrived and did a straightforward job. He fixed the pipe correctly. After that, I had to prepare for an exam at work. It felt like a test for my ability. I had to hold a meeting with my team later. My boss wants to discuss a case that is almost criminal in nature. A surgeon often deals with complex problems; my problem was much simpler. I always try to do my best}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day's End Reflection[/center]\nFriend: How was your day? You sounded a bit impatient this morning.\nMe: It was a bit of chaos early on. My neck was sore, and my room was messy! But the plumber fixed the pipe, which was straightforward. I even saw a tiny ant walking on the skyscraper outside. \nFriend: And your work? Was it like an exam?\nMe: In a way, yes. I had to answer correctly. My boss isn't an impolite person, but the discussion required a lot of focus. I hope my experience helped to provide the truth of the situation. \nFriend: Sounds like you showed great admiration for the challenges today. It’s important to be sensible even when things are difficult."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 59,
    "text1":
        "{r:The scenery outside my window was beautiful today. I prepared my baggage for a short trip. Unfortunately, my car had a small problem. My path will take me north, then east of the city. I have family living south and west. The directions are clear, and I have a map. I hope the weather will be good for traveling}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:At home, I keep food in the fridge. I also have some beer inside. Sometimes, a feeling of depression can come, but I always find happiness again. It’s a battle that happens inside me. There is often a big difference between sadness and joy. I believe in trying to feel good every day. Life is full of such moments}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:In old stories, a king often ruled a kingdom. They sometimes built strong walls, like a prison, to keep bad people away. I enjoy looking at art in the city museum. There are countless beautiful pictures and statues. It shows the feelings and ideas of people from long ago. These creations are full of history and meaning}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My nephew is a gamer. He spends a lot of time playing games. He likes games about a cowboy in the old West. The probability of winning a game is often small, but he enjoys the challenge. His total score is always very high. He believes that practice makes perfect, and he always tries to get the best result}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Short Trip and Thoughts[/center]\nFriend: How was your trip? The scenery must have been lovely!\nMe: It was great! I had my baggage with me, ready for adventure. Unfortunately, the journey was short. I traveled north and then east. I saw a happy kid playing. \nFriend: Did you stay in a hotel?\nMe: Yes, it was nice. It had a fridge! I put my beer inside. I thought about the king from an old story I read. That story had a sad part about a prison.\nFriend: And how did you feel?\nMe: No depression! Only happiness! It’s important to find that between the good and bad. I even saw some art in a small village. There were countless pieces. I even saw a gamer playing a game about a cowboy. The probability of finding so many interesting things was small, but it was a good trip. The total experience was excellent."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 60,
    "text1":
        "{r:I felt a terrible sickness this morning. I was too lazy to get out of bed, but there was a good reason I had to. My small business needed me. I looked at the long rope hanging near the door; this line was for something important. That was really difficult, but I had to start. I had almost no time to rest}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:There was an issue with a new member of our team today. I had to introduce him to everyone. He seemed shy, which was a pity. He spoke about his home kingdom and a long war that happened there many years ago. It showed the power of history. He told us a story about a prisoner who found freedom. These stories were very interesting. That was a deep conversation}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My friend had a big surgery last week, and it was a serious issue. I went to provide some help. It was really important to be there. I saw a kid in the hospital who was almost crying. This child had a small sickness. It made me feel a lot of pity. I believe in strong religious guidance during difficult times. That belief gives people strength. These are hard moments for many}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Our small business aims to provide clear guidance. We draw a line under old problems. The power of a good plan is great. We had an issue with a broken rope yesterday, but we fixed it quickly. We know how to deal with problems correctly. This means we are almost always ready. That makes our work straightforward. These are the things that help our team succeed}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day of Challenges and Help[/center]\nFriend: How was your day? Did you really feel bad this morning?\nMe: Yes, I had a sickness, and felt so lazy. But I had a reason to get up. My business had an issue with a new member.\nFriend: Oh, that's a pity. Did you have to introduce them?\nMe: Yes. They spoke about their kingdom and a war from long ago. It showed the power of a story. I also heard a kid was in the hospital for a surgery. That’s why I had to provide some help there, too. It was almost too much.\nFriend: This sounds like a lot for one day! Did you use that long rope for anything?\nMe: No, that rope is for another day. But I made sure to draw a line under all the completed tasks. These challenges make us stronger."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 61,
    "text1":
        "{r:I saw a bird with a long tail today. That bird was a beautiful one. It was building a nest in the big tree. This bird is a common species in our state. I also saw a man with a big moustache. He was wearing new pants. He seemed like a kind one. The sight of the bird made me feel peaceful. It's important to find moments to relax}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:My work for the firm is sometimes difficult. The main subject for today's meeting was growth. I had to calculate the numbers very carefully. The person who prepared the report was a talented one. I wrote an article about our new goals. It was a good one, I think. Shyness can be a problem for some people, but it is possible to grow past it. The company's goal is to grow, mostly in the north}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:An artist can create powerful images. Some of them show violence, which can be unbelievable to see. This art often tries to emphasize a point. Anyway, it can be a strong statement about the world. I saw a picture of an eagle with a long tail. That bird was a powerful one, almost like a symbol. The sight of it made me think deeply about power in nature}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:This question is an easy one. That question is a difficult one. These questions are about the subject of life. Those questions are about science. I like this red pen more than that blue one. These old books are better than those new ones. My small dog has a short tail, but my neighbor’s dog has a long one. I saw a bird making its nest. That nest was a large one}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day of Art and Thought[/center]\nFriend: Did you see the new art exhibition? It's a really interesting one.\nMe: Yes, I did! There was a painting of a man with a big moustache. He wore colorful pants. That one was very striking.\nFriend: And the birds? I heard there were many species.\nMe: Many! I saw a small bird with a long tail building a nest. That one was very busy. It made me want to relax. The artist seemed to emphasize the peace of nature. \nFriend: What was the main subject of the exhibition?\nMe: It was mostly about the human spirit. Some pieces showed violence, which was unbelievable to see. Anyway, it was a powerful statement about our state. Did you have to calculate anything for your firm today?"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 62,
    "text1":
        "{r:From my window, I had a beautiful view of the city. I saw some trees and some old buildings. A young boy was playing outside. The people here show great hospitality. There is some good energy in this place. I like to see the green nature outside. I noticed some dust on the shelf, but it was a minor issue. I hoped to recover from my tiredness soon}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:We had a meeting about a minor problem in our working system. There was some confusion, and some people spoke against the new plan. I tried to make a reasonable statement to explain my point. There wasn't any clear answer at first. The basis of the problem was hard to find. We decided to keep working to recover from this issue. Is there anything else we can do?}",
    "text3":
        "{r:Sometimes, a feeling of fury can rise when things go wrong. But it’s important to keep calm. Our team needs to perform well to celebrate success. We need some good ideas. Is there any new plan? Our leader always says to act in a reasonable way. There is some good sense in that idea. The nature of our work is to solve problems, not create them. We want to recover quickly}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The new park offers a wonderful view. It has some green grass and some colorful flowers. The local system of parks is greatly valued by the community. They keep it clean. Is there any litter on the ground? No, not any. A curious boy was looking at an ant. The nature around us can teach us many things. We should celebrate these gifts. We are always learning something new}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day's Events[/center]\nFriend: Did you see any good view today?\nMe: Yes, I did! From my window, I saw some beautiful nature. But I also saw some dust on the floor.\nFriend: Oh, that's a minor issue. Is there anything else I can do to help you recover?\nMe: No, thank you. I am already feeling better. We had some problems at work. Some people spoke against our new system.\nFriend: That can cause some fury.\nMe: It can! But I tried to make a reasonable statement to explain my point. I hope we can celebrate a good result soon. Our hospitality will be seen. I was curious to know if there was any real anger. Our goal is to keep peace. It greatly helps our business."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 63,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our small community is situated near a large river. There is no large hotel here, and we have no loud music. We try to live without any noise. During the hot summer, we find relaxation in the cool water. We have no garbage on the streets; we want no waste. Our aim is to live in peace. There aren't any big problems here, that is true}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The leaders who govern our city hold weekly meetings. They always include all opinions. No small matter is left unsaid. We have not any easy answers for every problem. However, they try to separate the big issues from the small ones. There is no simple solution for some problems. We have no doubt that they work hard for us}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Sometimes, I feel lonely, but it's only for a short time. I have a happy memory of my childhood. No sad story can change that strong feeling. I have no fear when I am in my safe home. I have a soft blanket that keeps my body warm at night. During the cold season, I always use it. There isn't any better feeling than being warm and safe}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I wanted to enter the old building, but there was no door. How many rooms does it include? None. It is an empty space. There was no light inside. No one was there, so I could not ask any questions. I had no phone to call anyone. What was the charge for this trip? There was no charge at all. It was free, but I found no satisfaction there}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Quiet Town's Life[/center]\nFriend: How many people live in your community? Are there any hotels?\nMe: There are many people, but no hotels at all. We have no large buildings here. This town is situated between green hills.\nFriend: How do the leaders govern?\nMe: They hold meetings, and they try to include everyone. There is no waste of time. However, there aren't any quick changes. They take their time. \nFriend: And what about relaxation?\nMe: There is no lack of it! We have no stress here. I have no bad memory of this place. If you ask who helps people here, I can say no one is left out. There isn't any lonely person. How many good stories do I have? Countless! But I have no blanket to share with you, it's just for my body."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 64,
    "text1":
        "{r:I wanted to join a club, but its membership was very expensive. It was pretty clear that it was not worth the money for me. The entrance to the building was small, and there wasn't anybody inside. Nobody was there to help. The whole situation seemed strange. I didn't see anything that made me want to join. I had no idea why there was no crowd. Nothing felt right about it}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The city government tried to solve the traffic problem. This situation did require a new plan. They did not allow anybody to drive too fast. They said nothing about future changes, however. Nobody knew what would happen next. They wanted to add a new road, but there was no space within the city. This was a rare case for them. It affected many people's livelihood}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our country's history has several memorable events. Nobody can forget the time when we won the big game. There wasn't anything more exciting that year. The level of happiness was high. However, there was also a sad case from the past; a famous leader went to prison. No one liked that part of our past. I didn't see anybody happy about that memory}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My livelihood depends on my work. I try to spend my time wisely. Nothing is more important than hard work for me. If there isn't anything to do, I will find a new task. I didn't ask anybody for help today. I wanted to solve my problems myself. This is a common social rule I live by. I will allow myself to rest later. No one can tell me what to do}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Challenging Week[/center]\nFriend: How was your week? Did anything new happen?\nMe: Nothing much, really. I didn't see anybody special. I wanted to ask about the club membership, but no one was at the entrance to help me.\nFriend: That's a pity. What about your work?\nMe: There was a strange situation regarding a rare case. We had to solve a difficult problem. Nobody knew the answer at first. The government has a new rule now. It is a new level of control. They don't allow anybody to do certain things. It felt like nothing was easy.\nFriend: That sounds like it would require a lot of time. Did you have to add anything to the report?\nMe: Yes, I had to add several details. It was a memorable week, but nothing I would want to repeat soon. I did not spend my time well this week, but I hope to recover next week."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 65,
    "text1":
        "{r:We started a search in the large green field. There was somebody important missing. For a moment, nobody knew where to look. We needed to find him quickly. There was nothing more important than this rescue. We hoped he did not try to escape anywhere alone. We had to find him somewhere. This was a true test of our human skills. We had to remain calm}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Our team worked separately, each teammate looking in a different area. There wasn't anybody who wanted to stop. We faced a difficult process. There seemed to be no exit from the big problem. We had nothing easy to do. We aimed to reach our goal within an hour. Something in the distance caught my eye, but it was just a small bird among the trees}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:This rescue mission, including the search, had a secondary purpose: to educate new team members. It was a chance to teach them how to control a tough situation. There was no problem with any disability for our team; we were all strong. We wanted to serve our community well. Nobody wanted to fail. It was a good lesson, showing that nothing is impossible with good teamwork}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:After the rescue, I went to the drugstore to buy something for my head. It was a small thing. There was nobody I knew there. I didn't go anywhere else after that. I just wanted to relax. The whole process taught me a lot. We had to control our feelings. I felt like a true human after that hard work. We did not need anything more}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day's Events[/center]\nFriend: Did you find somebody in the field today?\nMe: Yes, we did! After a long search. It was a difficult rescue.\nFriend: Was there anything broken?\nMe: No, nothing broken. But for a moment, we thought he might escape somewhere. There was no clear exit.\nFriend: How many people helped?\nMe: Many! Every teammate helped. Nobody gave up. We had to control the whole process. \nFriend: Did you go anywhere after that?\nMe: I went to the drugstore to buy something small for myself. It was really important to remain calm among the chaos. This was a big lesson to educate us all. We had to serve the community, and we reached our goal. Nothing was easy, but we succeeded."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 66,
    "text1":
        "{r:Every morning, I start new research. All the steps must be correct. The price of this work is high, but it is worth it. I need to calculate every detail. According to the plan, we will return to the city by evening. This project is a major one. We have to maintain a good rate of work. Every day, I learn something new. All my books are open}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:In our society, everybody has a role. All citizens must follow the rules. This is a basic requirement. The former leader was a good one. He used to emphasize the importance of peace. We had a major decision to make. Except for one person, everybody agreed. It's important to maintain calm, even when there is strong disagreement. All our ideas must be clear}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I looked everywhere for my phone charger. It was not on the table, not in my bag, nowhere. I had to pull out every drawer. Everything felt messy. This was a challenging process. I need it for my work. My phone is almost dead. The main subject of my search was the charger. I need to examine every corner of the room. It’s a common issue}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:A new mixture of ideas will lead us to success. We need to add additional support for every team member. We will join a new firm. We will raise our country's flag high. All the people will watch. Every person will feel happy. This is a powerful statement about our future. We must maintain our strong spirit. Our research is the basis of our success. Every piece of work helps}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Project's Progress[/center]\nFriend: Is everything ready for the new project? \nMe: Almost! Every report is complete. All the numbers are correct. We need to calculate the total cost. \nFriend: Did you find your charger? I looked everywhere for mine yesterday.\nMe: Yes, I found it! It was under some books. Anyway, everybody in the team is working hard. We have to maintain a fast rate. \nFriend: What is the major subject of this new research?\nMe: It's about a new species of plant. We need to emphasize its benefits. All our efforts will lead to success. Except for a few small issues, everything is on track. We will return tomorrow. We want to join the winning team."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 67,
    "text1":
        "{r:The city streets are often crowded. Most cars move slowly here. Some people are always awake, even at night. The police play an important role in maintaining order. All of them work hard. No noise is allowed after midnight. Most of the buildings are tall. Every season brings a new image to the city. I love to describe these changes}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Good education is key for humanity. Most children start school at a young age. Some of them learn very quickly. Formerly, not every child could go to school. Now, the majority of kids have this chance. Only a small minority do not. All of us want to see more progress. No easy solutions exist for every problem. I want to emphasize that education is for everyone}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I had to pick a couple of apples from the tree. Most of them were red. Some of my friends like green ones. All of these fruits tasted sweet. Half of them were for my family. This made my mind feel at ease. There is nothing better than fresh food. I tried to cover the food with a cloth to keep it clean. No insects were allowed near it. Most of the time, this works}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Our city tries to bring peace. Most citizens want a calm life. Some of the rules help to describe how we should live together. No one wants war. It is a certain truth. The solutions are often simple ones. If you have a sickness, a doctor can help you recover. All doctors play a vital role in our society. Most of their work is very important for all of us}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A City's Changing Face[/center]\nFriend: The city is very crowded these days. Most of the people are moving fast.\nMe: Yes, and the police have a difficult role. All of them try to keep order. Have you seen any changes in the education system?\nFriend: Yes, I have. Most of the schools are getting better. Formerly, some of the old buildings were not good. Now, the majority of kids have a chance to learn.\nMe: That brings peace to my heart. How many kinds of trees did you pick?\nFriend: I picked a couple of small ones. Half of them are for my garden. I hope they grow well. \nMe: That sounds lovely. It's a simple idea that brings happiness. I believe this is good for humanity. Most of the time, I feel awake at night, thinking about such things. No solution is easy. All doctors do a great job."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 68,
    "text1":
        "{r:Every morning, I think about my position at work. Each day brings a special opportunity. I want to be a sincere worker. None of my ideas are for my own benefit. I try to make a new record of my progress. Each solution for my problems is written down. Every small success makes me happy. I simply want to do my best. There is no other option}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:This new equipment was very costly. None of the team members wanted to buy it at first. However, it proved to be an effective solution. Now, each of us can work faster. Every customer is happy with the result. We need to cooperate to make this work. We have a clear description of how to use it. There are many options, but this one is the best. None of them are bad}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My city is known for its brick houses. Each house is unique. Every guest who visits loves them. I sat between two old buildings, looking at the view. Among these houses, there is a small garden. Every flower there is beautiful. None of these old traditions should be forgotten. We try to land new businesses here. Every new project is a welcome one}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:A doctor can prescribe medicine. Each doctor has their own way to do it. None of them will give you something bad. They want to find an effective solution for your sickness. Every patient is important. This medicine is affordable for most people. There is no other option that works as well. They simply want to help. Every day, they work hard to provide good health}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A New Project and Choices[/center]\nFriend: We have a new project. Each candidate has a special opportunity to join.\nMe: That's great! What is the main subject? And is it affordable for everyone?\nFriend: It's about building a new community center. The plan is to use brick for the walls. None of the costs are too high. Each person can cooperate.\nMe: How many options do we have for the design?\nFriend: We have several, but none of them are final yet. We need to choose between two good ideas. Every detail is important.\nMe: Will it require new equipment?\nFriend: Yes, some. And we need to record every step of the process. Every guest will see it. We want to land a great design. This is an effective solution for the community's needs. Every single member will be happy. We simply need to make sure every promise is kept."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 69,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our small group went on a trip to learn about an old town that was over a century old. Its unique culture was famous. We had seen old evidence that many brave men and women lived here long ago. There was a simple rule to follow: no loud noises. It was likely that many old plant species still grew there. We hoped for a peaceful experience. Every child in our group was excited, and all the children carried small bags}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:As we walked further into the quiet forest, we saw one large wolf. It was a powerful sight, and we knew there were other wolves in this area. A tiny mouse ran quickly into a hole; we just hoped no mice would try to enter our camp at night. Near a small pond, a beautiful goose was swimming, and a group of geese sat on the grass. It seemed like a constant fight for their lives in the wild, but they all looked strong}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We continued our walk, thinking about the tough condition of wildlife. We knew we had to defend nature. I felt a small pain in one tooth, a minor issue. I reminded myself to clean my teeth well every day. We came to an old house, and I used my small knife to cut some fruit. We had several knives for different tasks. This was a challenging choice, as we wanted to preserve the natural state of everything}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Our guide, a good listener, explained the history of the place. He had hundreds of stories available to tell. He said that the current term for this area was 'protected zone'. There was almost no exception to the strict rule about leaving things untouched. We collected all the remaining evidence of human activity, wanting to remove it. We had good security measures to protect the area}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Thoughts about the Journey[/center]\nFriend: That was an amazing journey! The culture of that old town felt like a whole new century, didn't it?\nMe: It did! And the wildlife! Seeing those wolves and all the geese made me think about their lives. Did you see that little mouse?\nFriend: Yes, and I really hope no mice come to our tents! The forest was so peaceful, though. It's a fight to keep it that way.\nMe: True. Our guide, a great listener, had so many stories available. He even had a story about a knife and the importance of good teeth for the ancient people. We have a clear rule to defend places like this.\nFriend: And the children seemed to learn so much. I think the current condition of the area is great. Was there any evidence of damage left?\nMe: No, not any. The remaining areas were clean. They even had security for the plants. There was no exception to their rule. It's likely we'll return next term."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 70,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our team received a new proposal today. It was about a large project on the university campus. We had to decide which approach to take. Both methods seemed promising and could certainly help us exceed our goals. We agreed to act firmly and choose one of them. We believed both options were strong, and either would lead to a good result. Our main task was to make a wise choice for the entire region}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:However, both plans presented their own challenges. Neither approach was without problems. The first one would involve a lot of travel, and the second one would require a new device. My eyesight is not as good as it was, so working with small parts of a new device could be a challenge for me personally. We needed to ensure both options were productive for the long term. Neither plan seemed simple, but we had to pick one}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We had to seek an even better solution. We wanted to find something that would bring wealth to the community, not just profits for our firm. Additionally, we needed to make sure it was somewhat easy to manage. We brainstormed over a thousand ideas, hoping to find an exception to the rule that big projects are always hard. Neither option from the initial proposal felt completely right for our goals}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The performance of our team was strong, as we worked late into the night. We examined both plans again, side by side. Neither plan was perfect, but we needed to make a decision by the morning. The final task was waiting. As the sun began to rise, we walked toward the main gate of the campus. Both of us felt tired, but also a sense of accomplishment. We knew we had made a good choice, as both options were better than none}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Final Decision[/center]\nFriend: So, did you decide on a proposal for the new campus project? Which approach did you choose?\nMe: Yes, we did! After much thought, we chose the second one. Both approaches had good points, but neither was without its difficulties. For example, that second one will involve a new device.\nFriend: And what about your eyesight? Will that be an issue for the new device?\nMe: It's somewhat of a concern, but I will manage. We need both plans to be productive. We want to exceed expectations and bring wealth to the region. \nFriend: I hope you can seek success! And how was the team's performance?\nMe: Excellent! Both of us worked hard. We stayed at the gate until late, trying to finalize the plan. Neither of us wanted to leave until it was perfect. The final task is now clear."
  },
  {
    //i read the texts from lesson 71 and making gemeini check
    "lesson": 71,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our team was very excited to start the new project. We knew it would be a lot of fun, but also a big difficult task with a high chance to fail. We spent many hours thinking of ideas, and we had a lot of ideas for how to begin. Our goal was clear, and the lead author of the plan was currently making the final changes. There was much hope among us for a successful result}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The first part of the project felt like a true battle. There was much pain as we faced surprising problems. We had to show a lot of strength to continue. It was almost a disaster at one point, but we were able to avoid it totally. We heard from many viewers that they were watching our improvement carefully. We did not have much time to waste, so we pushed forward}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We asked for feedback from experts, and we received a lot of useful feedback. It helped us to secure our position. We found that we did not have much sugar for strength, but that was a minor detail. We simply needed to fill our minds with good ideas. We had many new fighters join our team, ready to help us win the 'battle.' Their support meant a lot to us}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:After weeks of hard work, we began to see improvement. There were many small celebrations within the team as we reached each small goal. Our curiosity about the final result grew with each passing day. We had invested much time and strength. The author of the plan was happy to see it all come together. We felt the project was currently on track to succeed}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Project's Success[/center]\nFriend: That project was a lot of fun, wasn't it? I know we had many long days.\nMe: Really! There was so much pain and strength involved. I remember thinking we might fail at one point. It felt like a battle without end.\nFriend: Yes, but we received a lot of feedback from the viewers, and it was mostly positive. That helped us to secure our position.\nMe: It did! And the author's ideas were great. We had many celebrations in the end. I had a lot of curiosity about whether we would reach our goal. \nFriend: We totally did! And there was so much excitement. We did not use much sugar, but we found a lot of strength. This project was not a disaster; it was a very big success."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 72,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our team had to represent the company at the big event. We knew we needed to focus our minds and use every bit of energy we had. There was only a little time left before the start. The employer gave us a few notes to read, which contained some key points. We had very little doubt in our hearts, as we had worked hard, but we knew the task was difficult. Our goal was to win}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:As the event began, we realized the path to success was not easy. There was a sudden drop in our confidence when we saw the strength of the other teams. Few people truly understood the natural challenges of this event. We learned that the ability to overcome failure was a common trait among champions. We needed courage and a little love for the game to overcome the difficult parts}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We decided to share our remaining energy with each other. It was evident that we had no right to make errors. Every factor was significant. We had a little luck on our side, but mostly it was pure hard work. We made very few mistakes, which helped us greatly. We tried to focus on each small task, not the whole picture, to maintain our strength}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The final round depended on one last shoot. The clock on the watch showed a little time remaining. We had few chances left to save our position. Every player felt the pressure. We had to trust what we learned. We held our breath, hoping for a good result. There was very little anything else we could do but watch and wait for the result}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Result[/center]\nFriend: That was a very difficult event! How did you feel?\nMe: It was tough! We had a little energy left at the end, but we gave it our all. We had to push really hard.\nFriend: I saw that! There were a few moments where it looked like a failure was possible.\nMe: Yes, it was evident. We knew we had no right to make mistakes, and the employer expects us to represent well. But we managed to save it.\nFriend: So, did you win?\nMe: We did! It was a real success. We learned that courage and a lot of focus are significant factors. We shared the win, and it felt so good. We have a little celebration planned for later."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 73,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our town was holding a competition to find the most popular new design for a public park. The first design was from a young man; it was quite bright and handsome, but perhaps a little too complex. The likelihood of building it was lower than for the second design. This second one was by an older architect, and it offered a stronger defense against bad weather. It was also more interesting to study, offering better solutions to common problems}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:We had to decide which design was better. The young man's design was similar to many others we had seen, but the older architect's plan was more unique. She was known for being very fluent in modern design principles. Despite some initial concerns, we found her plan to be more careful and practical. We believed it would protect the trees and plants better, making it a more effective choice for the park. Neither was worse than the other in terms of beauty, but one was more practical}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The financial aspect was also a major factor. Building the first design would have been more expensive, requiring an enormous fund to complete. The second design was much cheaper and more affordable, which was a huge advantage. Our stock of building materials was limited, so we needed a plan that didn't demand too much. The generous offer from the architect to use more natural, less costly materials made her plan even better}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The architect herself was a truly sincere person, always polite and never rude. She showed great courage in defending her ideas. Her approach felt nicer than the other candidate's. We had a further discussion about some optional details, and she was happy to adjust them. Her experience made her plan easier to understand for everyone on the committee. She certainly was a very brave and talented woman}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Decision and Its Impact[/center]\nFriend: So, which park design did the committee pick? Was the older architect's plan chosen?\nMe: Yes, it was! Her design was better than the other. It was more interesting and seemed more effective.\nFriend: That's great! Was it also cheaper?\nMe: Much cheaper! Building it would require less funding, which was a significant factor. Her approach was more careful with resources, and she was very generous with her ideas. The other design was beautiful, but it was more expensive and perhaps less popular.\nFriend: And the architect herself? Was she as sincere as they say?\nMe: Absolutely. She's nicer than anyone I've met recently, and very fluent in explaining her vision. Despite the difficulties, her courage and bright ideas won our hearts. There was no doubt this was the better choice for our society."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 74,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our new archaeological dig was on a truly gigantic piece of land, much bigger than any site we had explored before. The main path to the center was narrow, much narrower than the wide paths around the edge. The ground itself, after some initial treatment, was still quite rough, a bit rougher than we had expected. We noticed a very shiny object near an old tree, which was a bit more interesting than the usual stones we found}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The initial digging proved to be more painful than usual, because the soil was very dry and hard. It was much harder than the soft soil at our last site. We had to work together, and the involvement of every team member was essential. Our focused efforts were necessary to break through the tough ground. The work was much more difficult than digging in the wet fields we knew, but we had to continue}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our representative from the museum informed us about the budget. He said that this dig was more expensive than our previous projects, despite our best efforts to find savings. We needed to be completely honest about every cost. Buying new equipment was also more costly than we thought. We hoped the results would be worth it, because the money situation was more critical than ever}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:One day, we found an ancient tool. It was made of a smooth stone, much smoother than anything we had seen before. At first, some of the junior researchers seemed a bit dumb, not understanding its importance. But our senior doctor quickly identified it. Near the tool, there was a shallow pool of water, which was a bit shallower than the maps indicated. This discovery was much better than finding just old pieces of brick}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The End of the Dig[/center]\nFriend: So, how was the big dig? Was it more difficult than you expected?\nMe: It was much more difficult than our last one, especially because the ground was so dry and rough. Our involvement had to be more focused than ever. We needed to show great strength.\nFriend: And the budget? I heard it was more expensive than planned.\nMe: Yes, the treatment of the site was more costly than we thought. We had less savings than we hoped, so we needed to be completely honest. But the findings were better than expected.\nFriend: Did you find anything shiny?\nMe: We found a very old, shiny tool! It was made of smooth stone, much smoother than modern tools. It was a gigantic step for our research! The results are much more important than the costs. This dig was certainly a challenging but rewarding experience."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 75,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our new security device was designed for protection. It was a truly clever invention, not as ancient as the old alarms, but its quality was just as high. We had to prepare it carefully before its first big test. The system's availability was important; it needed to be as active as possible, twenty-four hours a day. The launch date had to be timely and efficient for everyone involved}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our engineers, all courageous and intelligent individuals, worked under enormous pressure. They weren't as silent as they usually were; there was a lot of talking. The availability of coffee was not as much as they wanted, but they tried. Each engineer was as focused as the next, ensuring every detail was perfect. Their effort was truly valuable, showing their full strength}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Suddenly, we found a small rat in the test area. It was not as big as a cat, but it caused a minor problem. We had to identify its path and ensure it didn't damage the device. The situation was not as serious as a real crisis, but it tested our quick thinking. We found the solution was as simple as closing a small hole. The quality of our quick response was the same as expected from our trained team}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Successful Launch[/center]\nFriend: The launch of the new security system went well! Was its performance as good as you hoped?\nMe: Of course! It was as accurate as we designed it to be. The protection it offers is as effective as any other system on the market.\nFriend: And the engineers? Were they under a lot of pressure?\nMe: They were, but they're courageous people. They weren't as silent as usual, but their focus was incredible. Their dedication was the same as mine. The quality of their work was surprising.\nFriend: Did you have any unexpected issues?\nMe: Just a small one – a rat! It was not as big as I thought, but we had to identify it quickly. Thankfully, the solution was as simple as closing a small opening. We had to prepare for everything!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 76,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our small team decided to establish a new art gallery, hoping it would become the best in the city. We had a very optimistic approach to the project. Our preparation was detailed, and we focused on every particular aspect. We wanted the gallery to be the most elegant and inviting place. The art pieces themselves varied greatly, from very plain to incredibly fancy designs. We believed this was the easiest way to attract many visitors}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Finding the best spot for the gallery was a challenge. The city had some harsh conditions for new businesses. Our staff, which included both bald and slim men and women, worked tirelessly. We wanted to avoid the worst possible result, which would be to fail. Whatever happened, we wanted to succeed. The building we found was a bit dusty, but it had the most perfect atmosphere for art}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We knew that filling the gallery with art would be the most expensive part. Our goal was to show some of the oldest and most valuable pieces. We searched for art that would indicate the beauty of our culture. We found one ancient painting that was the most beautifil, but also the most costly. We decided to transport it carefully in a special van. It would certainly be the most interesting piece in our collection}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Our affection for this project grew each day. We felt pride in every detail, even the least significant. We decided that whenever we faced a problem, we would discuss it openly as a team. We wanted the gallery to be not just a building, but a place that brought joy to everyone. It was the best feeling to see our dreams slowly becoming a reality}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Grand Opening[/center]\nFriend: The grand opening of the gallery was fantastic! It's truly the most elegant place in the city.\nMe: Thank you! We tried to make it the best. Our optimistic approach really worked. And the staff was incredible.\nFriend: The particular piece in the center, the ancient painting, is the most interesting! Was it the most expensive too?\nMe: It was the most expensive definitely, but also the most important. It's one of the oldest pieces we have. We moved it with a special van.\nFriend: And the building, it looks so clean, but it was dusty when you found it, right?\nMe: Yes, it was dusty, but we worked hard. We didn't want the worst outcome. We made a lot of preparation and affection to make it perfect. It was the easiest decision to work with this team. We truly feel pride in this new gallery."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 77,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our new politician was preparing for the upcoming election. He had enough training and skill to speak well, but he knew he needed more. He wanted to move forward with grace and dignity. We discussed if he had enough confidence, and he said yes. He believed his ideas were abundant and strong enough to win. Every day, he made enough practice to perfect his speeches}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:However, the campaign had its challenges. We didn't have enough money for all our plans, and the amount of resources was not always sufficient. Our campaign office wasn't spacious enough for all the new staff members. There was also not enough stuff to decorate the office well. We tried not to complicate things more than necessary, but logistics were always a concern. We really hoped to have enough of everything to make this campaign a success}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We held a thorough analysis of the public's opinion. The benefit of our campaign message was clear enough for most viewers. There was a certain sweetness in the positive feedback we received. We felt that our arguments were sufficient to persuade voters. We allowed ourselves to laugh a little at the small problems, as long as they were not big enough to cause a disaster. We aimed to keep everything as simple as possible}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:As the election day approached, our candidate's message felt ripe enough for the public. He had done enough to explain his views. We made a final decision not to message any further, as there was not enough time. It was a fair trade of ideas in the public forum. He believed he was ready enough to face any question and felt confident in the outcome}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Election Day Opinions[/center]\nFriend: Well, the election is over. Do you think our politician did enough?\nMe: I certainly think so. He had enough training and skill to present his message clearly. His ideas were abundant enough to inspire many people.\nFriend: Do you think he had enough money for the campaign? I heard resources were tight.\nMe: We never had enough money to do absolutely everything, but the amount we had was sufficient. Our office wasn't spacious enough for everyone, but we made it work. We tried not to complicate things too much. We laughed a little at the small issues.\nFriend: And the analysis? Was the message ripe enough?\nMe: Yes, it was. The benefit of his platform was clear enough. He behaved with such dignity. He felt he had done enough to move forward and win. I'm proud of his efforts!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 78,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our small design team was trying to create a new building. John, the lead architect, was very ambitious, sometimes too ambitious for the project's budget. Mark, his partner, was a bit stubborn, and sometimes too stubborn to change his mind. We had a new member, Sarah, who was too skinny and looked a bit pale from working long hours. We hoped the project would gain popularity, but it was starting to feel too complicated for us}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The building's main design had too many small details, which made it too hard to build quickly. One day, an unusual problem appeared – an odd noise from the foundation. It was too loud to ignore. We worked actively to find a solution. It was a convenient moment that our best engineer was on site, because this issue was too strange for anyone else to understand. We needed to solve it quickly before it caused further delays}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The pressure of the deadline was becoming too much. Some team members became too jealous of each other's ideas, which created a dull atmosphere. We tried to stay calm and focus on the task. The situation was becoming too stressful for many of us. An unexpected request from the client to add a large new section to the building made everything feel even more difficult}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The new request was too expensive for our current budget. We tried to find a way to make it work, but the financial challenge was too great to overcome easily. The client, unfortunately, was being a bit dishonest about their expectations, or perhaps just careless with their numbers. Similarly, the project felt too big to finish on time without additional resources. It was clear we needed more help}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Difficult Choice[/center]\nFriend: How's the new building design coming along? Is it still feeling too complicated?\nMe: Yes, it's still too much for us. The new client request is too expensive for our budget, and the deadline is too tight.\nFriend: Oh, that's rough. Are people feeling too jealous of each other? I heard some rumors.\nMe: A little, yes. The atmosphere is somewhat dull because of the pressure. And the client's demands are too much to handle. They're being a bit careless with their requests, and maybe even dishonest.\nFriend: What about Mark? Is he still too stubborn?\nMe: He is. He won't change his mind easily. This project is too big to be solved by one person, and we need everyone's cooperation. I'm feeling tired too from all this stress."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 79,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our small theatre group prepared for our main performance on the stage. Every actor was truly skilled. Our ambition was great; we wanted to prove our talent to the entire city. The director explained our parts to us below the stage. We knew our individual acting styles might vary, but together we created a unified show. There was also a strong sense of generosity among the team}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:In the meantime, we had to make a trial performance. We worked hard to avoid any mistakes on the stage. We needed to reveal the story clearly to every viewer. The director stressed the impact of every gesture. Indeed, every small detail mattered. He asked us to guess what the audience would feel during the emotional song. We listened carefully to his advice}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our main goal was to deliver a strong message. We made a clear claim that this performance would be the best of the year. Our prominent lead actor practiced his lines tirelessly. He used his voice as a weapon, making sure every word reached the last row. We worked to make the entire show a powerful experience for all. We wanted to prove our dedication to the art}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:On the night of the premiere, the tension was high. We performed our song beautifully on the stage. We saw the impact of our art on the audience as they listened silently. The director watched from above, a proud smile on his face. He knew we had done our best. We successfully managed to avoid any major errors and delivered a truly memorable show}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Aftermath[/center]\nFriend: That was an amazing performance! The entire play was just perfect.\nMe: Thank you! We tried to make it the best. Our ambition was high. Did you like my song?\nFriend: I did! Your voice was a real weapon. The impact on the audience was obvious. You could see it on every face.\nMe: We worked hard to prove ourselves. There was indeed a lot of preparation involved. We wanted to avoid any issues on the stage. \nFriend: And the main actor? He was very prominent.\nMe: Yes, he is truly skilled. His generosity with his time also helped us. This was certainly our best show yet. We hope to reveal more great things in the future."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 80,
    "text1":
        "{r:The old house on the hill was often quiet, but sometimes a strange, scary noise would make you think someone was going insane. The local police usually received calls about it, but they seldom found any specific evidence. The main problem was the lack of honesty from a few witnesses. It seemed an unnecessary mystery, but it always bothered the town's adults. They hoped to discover the truth throughout the whole area}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Our small investigative team, which consisted of both adults and younger, skilled members, decided to look into the property itself. The work was very tough, but we always kept our optimistic approach. We rarely found anything significant on the surface, so we knew we needed to look deeper. The range of possible explanations was wide, and we just needed to find the right one. We could still hear some strange sounds inside the house}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:In the meantime, we discovered a hidden room. Some things there were truly beneficial to our investigation. There was a lot of old stuff hidden in a box, probably from a past party. We had to measure the room carefully and mention every detail. The police chief, an adult with much experience, already said this was the best evidence yet. This discovery would certainly shake the previous theories about the house}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The truth began to reveal itself. It was not a ghost, but an old ventilation system that would shake the entire house when the wind blew a certain way. It was a simple, natural explanation that made the previous fear seem unnecessary. We had just found the answer. We always believe that the simplest solution is often the right one. We decided to inform the public instead of keeping it a secret}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The End of the Mystery[/center]\nFriend: So, the mystery of the old house is solved! Was it scary?\nMe: Not anymore! It was just an old fan that would shake the house. We usually find simple explanations for such things. It was unnecessary to be so afraid. I mean, thinking it was something insane is easy when you don't know the truth.\nFriend: So, the strange noises were always the fan?\nMe: Yes, it was always the fan! We rarely find such simple solutions. We just found the proof. Our main goal was to discover the truth and bring some honesty to the situation. The adults in town are already feeling much better about it. It's beneficial for everyone to know the truth throughout the community."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 81,
    "text1":
        "{r:The old coach looked at a new cream. It was a commercial product, an item for your skin. They sold a big quantity of it. People said it was a great discovery. There were various kinds for the surface of your body. But the coach worried. He saw a sad reality: some people got cancer. The reason why was insufficient. It didn't make sense. His purpose was to find the truth. He thought, 'Bad ideas should not rule our lives.' He needed to beat this problem. He was particularly worried about the young generation. How would they exist if this continued? He knew he had to look ahead and be thoughtful. People tend to trust new things}.",
  },
  {
    "lesson": 82,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our city was preparing for a crucial election. The campaign manager, a senior member of our team, was a man of immense bravery. He would take full responsibility for every decision. He told us, 'We must be ready for any threat from our opponents.' He wanted to give the citizens a clear message about our future. We knew our actions were entirely focused on helping the public, not creating a victim}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:He always emphasized the importance of prevention over reaction. 'Don't spit out unverified information. Always have proof for every statement,' he'd say. He asked me to pass these new flyers to the volunteers. Later, he had me send the final report to our core partnership group. He wanted to show the citizens the truth and build trust. He believed honesty would earn us every vote}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:During a public debate, our candidate faced a direct threat. He felt a sudden dryness in his mouth and his nose twitched, but he maintained a smile. He wouldn't let this opponent make him a victim. He knew he had to bear the pressure and admit his past mistakes if necessary, but only with solid proof. The audience watched his every move, eager to see his response}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The debate was a success, and our candidate scored highly. The audience cheered, and his score was much better than the opponent's. Our campaign manager was incredibly pleased. 'I must get a special gift for him after this victory,' he decided. He also planned to buy some new equipment for the entire team. He wanted to give his appreciation to every member who contributed entirely to our success. He would show them his thanks clearly}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Election Victory and Future Plans[/center]\nFriend: The election was a clear win! How did you feel about the senior manager's leadership?\nMe: He was amazing! He showed incredible bravery against every threat. He truly earned the vote of every citizen. He never let us spit out false information; he always demanded proof.\nFriend: And the debate? Did he manage his emotions?\nMe: Absolutely. Even with a dry mouth and a twitching nose, he kept a smile. He wouldn't become a victim of his opponent's tactics. He had to tolerate intense pressure and admit only what was true.\nFriend: So, he was responsible for the entire campaign's success?\nMe: Entirely! He wants to give all the praise to the team. He's also planning to buy us new computer. He believes in prevention of future problems, so he's already planning our next steps. He wants to show us new ways to communicate with the audience. What a score for the team!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 83,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our team of experts planned to investigate the ancient ruins deep in the forest. We decided to depart at sunrise on Tuesday morning. Before we left, we had a brief debate on the best route. Our lead expert, who was born in 1975, reminded us that we solely had to focus on the research, and not boast about our past achievements. We wouldn't use any prepositions with 'this', 'next', 'last', 'every' in our reports}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The first night, we heard a distant bell ring at 9 o'clock. Later, a sudden storm began in the evening. We started to suffer from the cold. The flash of lightning would disturb our rest sometimes throughout the night. Our strict rule was that everyone must stay inside their tents after sunset. We had to treat one of our younger members who caught a fever; thankfully, she was partly recovered until morning}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We discovered layers of ash that indicated an ancient fire. We deemed this an important discovery. Our expert said that these ruins might have been the house of slaves. We were trying to find more artifacts in this area. We knew we didn't have spare time. We were confident we would reveal more secrets in a few days. This was our chance to make a truly significant discovery}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:One afternoon on Thursday, a wild monkey suddenly appeared and tried to disturb our work. We had to gently chase it. We continued our digging, focusing on an old wall. We looked up at sunset and saw the beautiful colors in the sky. We decided to admit to the authorities that we found something truly unique. We packed our things, knowing we would depart in two hours. It was an incredible journey}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Expedition's End[/center]\nFriend: So, how was the investigation? Did you depart at sunrise as planned?\nMe: Yes, on Tuesday. It was quite an adventure! We suffered from the cold at night sometimes.\nFriend: Did you find any ancient items?\nMe: We found a lot of ash from an old fire. Our experts deem it very important. We also saw a wild monkey on Wednesday!\nFriend: What about the lightning? Was it very bad?\nMe: It was intense in the evening, and it would disturb us. We had a strict rule about staying in tents. We had to treat one of our team members for a fever. But we didn't boast about our challenges. We partly finished our analysis; we'll finish in two weeks.\nFriend: So, you're back now. Will you reveal your findings soon?\nMe: Yes, we plan to publish our report in a month. We had to admit that the site was even older than we thought."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 84,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our new mission was to build a secure data center(ma'lumotlar markazi). Every participant had to comply with the strict security protocols from the very beginning to the final inspection. This was an important project for the company's future. We knew we had to thrive under enormous pressure. The project manager, who had been with the company since 2010, emphasized that all data security measures must be equally applied to everyone}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:We worked hard every day until midnight. The project manager warned us that if we didn't comply with the timeline, there would be a fine (penalty) for the entire team. We couldn't afford any disappointment from the client. Our goal was to maintain safety throughout the whole process. We had to judge every step carefully, ensuring no mistakes were made till the last minute}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:One senior participant was planning to retire by the end of the year. He had been a part of many successful missions since he graduated from the academy in 1995. We wanted to publish our findings and release the new system before his departure. There was a sudden cold in the room when we thought about him leaving, but his experience had been beneficial for many years}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The final phase became a tough nut to crack; we had to chew on difficult problems for hours. We took a short break and walked into the nearby forest to clear our minds. We would stare at the trees, trying to find solutions. We had to recall past experiences to overcome this obstacle. We knew we had been working on this critical problem for almost a month straight, and we wouldn't stop until it was solved}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Mission Accomplished[/center]\nFriend: The data center mission is complete! Did you finish on time?\nMe: Yes, we finished just before the deadline! We worked from early morning to late night for several weeks. Every participant had to comply fully.\nFriend: That's great! Was it a tough project?\nMe: Absolutely. It was a real nut to chew on, especially in the last week. We were worried about disappointment if we didn't release it on time. But the team managed to thrive.\nFriend: What about the fine? Did you get one?\nMe: No, thankfully not! We worked until the last minute, ensuring safety and quality. Our senior colleague, who will retire soon, said it was our best work since he joined the company. He's been with us for over 20 years, so that's a high score! We will publish the details next month."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 85,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our city faced a growing crisis. Before it became public, a secret investigation had begun. We made a deliberate attempt to recruit new people to help. We asked for full compliance from everyone involved. The spirit of the team was strong, and we felt ready to face a great challenge. We wanted to find solutions before the problem became bigger}.",
    "text2":
        "{r: During the first weeks of the investigation, we had to track many facts. While our small team worked tirelessly, the general attitude of the public fear. Many people were worried about their wages and daily labor. We noted that while we were collecting information, many citizens were still trying to understand the reality of the situation. We tried to give them hope}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:To find a recovery from this crisis, we needed to gain access to all necessary files. Therefore, we asked for special permission. We had to refer to past cases to understand the true object of the problem. This was not about gaining fame for ourselves; it was about saving the city. We rolled up our sleeves, knowing we had much hard work ahead of us}.",
    "text4":
        "{r: After weeks of intense work, the worst part of the crisis began. The departure of the main cause of the problem happened swiftly after our findings were published. The city felt a sense of freedom. Before resting, we reviewed all our actions. The strong spirit shown during this period was very important; it proved our ability to overcome great difficulties. We had beat the problem}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Reflecting on the Outcome[/center]\nFriend: That was quite a crisis the city went through. What did you learn during the investigation?\nMe: We learned a lot. Before it became public, we made a deliberate attempt to recruit a small team. Compliance was key, and everyone showed a good spirit.\nFriend: And while you were working?\nMe: We did a lot of labor. While we were tracking facts, the general attitude in the city was not good. Many were worried about their wages. We tried to find a way to help them.\nFriend: What happened after?\nMe: After we gained access to the main files, the recovery began. The departure of the core problem brought freedom. We had to refer to all our notes. It wasn't about fame, but about solving the problem. We succeeded!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 86,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our new client came right at the front door of our premise. My cousin, who works here, met him at the door. We took him into the big office. He sat in a chair, ready to talk about his needs. We gave him a variety of drinks, and he took a bottle of water. This workplace was always ready for important visits}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:He put the bottle with its label on the small table near him. We saw a thin scar on his cheek as he spoke. He pointed to a map on the wall, showing a wide desert area. He spoke of a long row of old trees along the coast where he wanted to build. He thought we should meet at a certain crossroad later to see the site}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our assumption was that the desert would be very dry, but he spoke of areas with much shade. He said, preferably, we should plan our visit in the early morning. We found some old maps in the company library that showed more facts of the coast. He said a small troop of workers was already in the area, making the place ready for the project. They were working in the bright sun}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:He told us a story about a man who was jailed near that desert site because of a strange problem. We all learned about the strict rules in that region. Our client felt good at our office, asking many questions. He liked the quiet air in the room. He said that every part of the workplace must be safe}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Planning the Desert Project[/center]\nFriend: So, the new client came today? Was he at the office?\nMe: Yes, he was at the front door when I came. My cousin met him at the door. He was in the meeting room for most of the morning.\nFriend: And the project? Is it in the desert?\nMe: That's right! He showed us a map on the wall. He wants us to work in a very dry area, but he says there's natural shade. He talked about a man who found himself in jail there once.\nFriend: Did he choose a certain meeting place?\nMe: Yes, he thought we should meet at a crossroad near the coast, preferably early. He spoke of a small troop of workers already in the area. He put his bottle on the table and shared many facts."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 87,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our new big project began in the old district of the city. It was a huge responsibility for all of us. We aimed to build a new factory where the old one stood. The ground around it was poor, but we had a good plan. We wanted to bring equality to job chances in this area. Everyone involved knew they had to be compliant with the new safety rules from the start}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:We often walked on the sidewalk near the project site. From a high slope in the nearby hills, we could see the whole district. The horizon was wide and clear. We drove to the border of the district to check the survey points at a small farm. Near the shore of the river, there was a big cliff with a strange feature. It was a good spot for a break}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our main meeting room felt like a big classroom in the old factory building. We had a dozen old maps and plans spread out on the table. We had to use our brains to solve many problems. One plan showed a way to replace the old water pipes that were at the bottom of the old wall. We needed to be smart about every part of the work}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:We worked hard at the factory site every day. Everyone was compliant with the strict rules, knowing their responsibility. There was a real possibility that the project would finish early if we kept this speed. We cleared the ground where the new building would stand. In the evenings, we would sometimes relax at the small theater in the next street, talking about the day's progress and planning for the next}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Success in the District[/center]\nFriend: The new factory project in your district is huge! How do you feel about the responsibility?\nMe: It's big, but we are all compliant and ready. We want to bring equality to the area. We work at the site every day from morning to evening.\nFriend: Did you use the old building's plans?\nMe: We found a dozen old plans and they felt like a classroom in the old factory. We used our brains to make new plans. We decided to replace some old parts.\nFriend: What about the surrounding area?\nMe: We walked on the sidewalk a lot. From the slope, you can see the whole horizon and the cliff near the shore. There's a true possibility for this district to become great. We meet often at the theater to celebrate our small wins."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 88,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our new mission was to find an old cure for a big problem. We had a date for our trip. Our target was a small village far from the city. There was a lack of clear roads, so we had to walk across hard land. Our previous attempts did not bring good results, but we were willing to try again. We made sure to deliver our plans clearly to all members}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:We walked up a high slope and saw a fence behind an old house. We went through a thick forest, where old tree sticks lay under our feet. We saw an animal run over a fallen tree. It was obvious that this path was not used by many. We had to handle our bags carefully to avoid any trouble. The shape of the trees changed as we went further}.",
    "text3":
        "{r: At one point, we saw a small building opposite us. We could feel a strange presence there. We looked at a small screen on our tool, which showed a scale of the land's features. We hoped to gain facts about the old cure. The volume of our voices was low. We had no shame in asking for help if needed}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:We moved along a small path, past old stones. Our leader had to grab a long stick to help him walk up a small hill. He didn't blink even once. We were willing to walk all day to deliver our report. We knew that people who reside in the small village would be waiting for us. There was an old map rolled up in his hand, showing the path we were on}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Journey's End[/center]\nFriend: How was your search for the old cure? Did you reach your target?\nMe: Yes, we did! We walked across a wide field and up many hills. Our previous failures made us more willing to try hard this time.\nFriend: What was the hardest part?\nMe: Going through the forest. There were old sticks under our feet, and a long fence behind some trees. But it was obvious we had to handle it. We had to communicate clearly too.\nFriend: And the village? Did you find what you needed?\nMe: Yes! We saw a building opposite us. We looked at a screen to gain facts. The people who reside there were very kind. We were happy to deliver the news. We rolled up our maps and started our walk back. No shame in feeling tired after such a trip!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 89,
    "text1":
        "{r:I was fedupwith the noise in the city, so I decided to take a holiday. I heard about a quiet place by the coast on the radio. I usually travel by subway, but this time I chose to go by train. I arrived at the small station feeling good. I had a small bag with me, and nothing much else. I was ready to observe the wild nature}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The first day, I learned about the history of slavery in the past here. It was a sad story. I felt it was important to know. I found a small old facility where they used to teach terms to new people. I saw a wild animal emerge from the trees. It was a beautiful sight. I had a book with me, which had many old pictures on its pages}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I spent hours just watching the wild birds and animals. I felt great envy for their simple life, without human problems. I listened to the birds singing on the branches. There was a small vehicle parked by the old road. I wondered about its story. I was strictly on my own, just with my thoughts, enjoying the quiet presence of nature}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My responsibility during this holiday was to just rest. I did not want to think about work. I spent some time at a small shop where they had many local sales. I even saw a unique replacement part for an old tool. The owner spoke about his life with a smile. I went back to my little house by the river on foot, thinking about all the simple beauty around me}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Reflecting on My Time[/center]\nFriend: So, how was your holiday? Did you enjoy it?\nMe: Yes, I did! I was fedupwith city noise, so I went by train. I got there on time at the station.\nFriend: What did you do there?\nMe: I learned about the history of slavery and saw a new animal emerge. I also saw an old facility and a vehicle parked by it. I read a book on the beach with a cup of tea.\nFriend: Sounds good! Did you feel free?\nMe: Yes! I enjoyed being without any big plans, just watching the wild life. I felt some envy for their simple existence. I found a local shop at the end of the road that had many good sales. It was a great replacement for my usual busy life."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 90,
    "text1":
        "{r:I was fed up with waiting for things to change. I felt a bit childish for being so furious about the long delay. The idea of going abroad seemed like a good way to relax my mind. I was afraid of starting something new, but I was incapable of making a plan. It was important to promote my own peace. I started thinking about finding a new place to reside, perhaps far from here}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:My friend was angry with the boss for not listening. He was fond of old stories about great treasures. I could see he was envious of those who found fame easily. He always had great faith in the good of people. He felt hopeless sometimes, but he was always good at helping others. He often spoke about helping to feed the hungry, showing his kind spirit. He was married to a very patient woman}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I was aware of my own limits, and I was conscious of the need to be tolerant with others. We found a small sample of old gold, a tiny treasure, in the old building. It was quite different from what we expected. We spoke about finding a way to contribute to the local museum. It was nice of the local leader to show us so much about the history of the district}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The cruel reality was that the journey abroad would be hard. But I was capable of handling it. I was engaged in planning every step, from the start. I was bad at remembering all the small facts without writing them down. I was sorry for any trouble I might cause to my family by leaving. My goal was to promote a better life for myself, free from past problems}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A New Path[/center]\nFriend: So, you decided to go abroad? Are you still fed up with everything?\nMe: Yes, I was furious about the past, and I felt a bit hopeless. But I decided I'm capable of starting fresh. I'm not afraid of making big changes now.\nFriend: And your family? Are they angry with you?\nMe: No, they are fond of my plans. My cousin is even interested in joining later. My mother always had great faith in me. I am aware of their support.\nFriend: What are you hoping to find?\nMe: I want to find a new treasure, perhaps a small sample of a better life. I'm conscious of the need to be tolerant with myself and others. It's nice of them to understand. I will contribute my best to this new path, and I am good at making plans."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 91,
    "text1":
        "{r:Every morning, I wake up early, even before the light comes. I like to get up quietly not to disturb my family. I usually sit down at the kitchen table with a book. My little brother often comes in to the kitchen soon after me. He sometimes tries to go out and play in the garden right away, but it is too early}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:My father then gets in his car to go to work. He usually comes out of the house at the same time every day. Later, my mother and I decide to eat out for lunch, a small good thing for us. We walked down the street to our best place. My mother had to tell me to calm down my happy spirit as we walked along the path}.",
    "text3":
        "{r: At the place, we saw a small child who was furious about something. He kept trying to stand up on his chair. His mother had to tell him to sit down many times. When she asked him to speak up and tell her what was wrong, he only cried. He tried to run away from the table, but his father quickly grabbed him. He then tried to put down a small object on the floor, but it fell down instead}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:After lunch, we had to go back home to be with our dog. My mother remembered she had to call back her friend who left a message. Our friend came by and wanted to give away some more apples from his garden. We thanked him and told him to come back any time. The sun was going down, and the day was coming to an end}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day's Events[/center]\nFriend: So, what did you do today? Did you get up early?\nMe: Yes, I wake up early and get up right away. I sit down to read a bit before others come in. Then my father goes out to work.\nFriend: And you and your mother?\nMe: We decided to eat out for lunch. We had to tell a child to calm down at the place. He kept trying to stand up and then wanted to run away. He tried to put down an object, but it fall down.\nFriend: Did you come back home then?\nMe: Yes, we had to go back. My mother had to call back her friend. And our friend came to give away some apples. It was a good day, and the sun went down as we finally rested."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 92,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our team had a big task. We needed to find out why the old machine kept stopping. We decided to look around the factory first, to see if anything was obvious. My friend, Tom, had to look after the small parts. We told him to hold on and wait for our main report. He said he could get along well without much help, which was good. We were willing to go on working until we found the problem}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:As we worked, a small bird decided to fly over our heads, right through the open door. It made us turn around and look up. The bird then tried to climb over a high box in the corner. We knew we could not give up now; we had to figure out what was wrong with the machine. We tried to keep on working, but the bird was a bit disturbing}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Later, the machine suddenly started to work again. It was a strange moment. We had tried everything and then it just started. It felt like we come across the answer by chance. We knew we had to go on making sure it would not fall down again. We found a small report about the machine from a previous owner. It was a good thing to find out}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:One young worker was feeling tired and said he might drop out of the task if it became too hard. We told him to hold on and stay strong. We could not give up yet. We had to keep on working to find a permanent cure. He said he might end up feeling sick if he did not rest. We told him that we needed him to go on with us}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day's Challenges[/center]\nFriend: So, what happened in the end? Did you figure out the problem?\nMe: Yes, we did! A small wire was loose. We replaced it, and the machine was good again. We learned that even when things are hard, it is important not to give up.\nFriend: Did you celebrate your success?\nMe: We all went to eat out after our hard work. We were glad to have each other to get along with, and we knew we could look after any new problems that came our way. There was no shame in being tired after such a day!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 93,
    "text1":
        "{r:The annual gathering was a big affair in our district, and people from a broad background came. Previously, we had some problems, but this year, there was a strong willingness to make it perfect. Many teams wanted to compete, so we planned for a high speed event. Everyone was excited because it was a time for friends to see each other}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:There was one small disadvantage: the old sound system did not work well. We had to reject the idea of using it, and find a new one quickly. We had to make people aware of this problem, so they would not be disappointed. Some wanted to ignore the issue, but it was too important. We needed a strong voice because the area was large}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The male participants started to gather at the front of the stage. A big wave of cheers went over the crowd, and the good spirit began to spread. We wondered if the speed would be too high or just right for the contest. It was obviously going to be a close game. The energy was great because everyone felt ready to compete}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:After the first quarter of the games, we did a quick review. Many people brought a small gift for the winners, and they placed them under the big tree. Some winners had to go back to their families early, so we gave them their gifts then. It was a fair affair because the judges were very strict about the rules, and no one could cheat}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Day of Competition[/center]\nFriend: How was the annual gathering? Did many people gather?\nMe: Yes, it was a very broad affair! People from all backgrounds came, and many were willing to compete. So, the speed was high.\nFriend: Did you have any problems?\nMe: Previously, we had a small disadvantage with the sound, but we had to reject the old system because it was broken. We needed to make people aware of it, or they might ignore it.\nFriend: And the results?\nMe: The male participants were very good. We did a review after the first quarter. The best player got a big gift, and we were all happy because of the good spirit that spread among us."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 94,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our new chief came to the office. When he arrived, his first task was to hire new people. We knew this job would extend for a long time. We spoke about bringing more female workers into the team. Our daily aim was to work hard. The new project had no limit, so we hoped for big results}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:He believed that careful observation was key. While we were in the field, we tried to note every small feature. We learned about the cruelty of leaving trash on the ground. Our consciousness grew as we saw the bad influence of human actions. We tried not to destroy anything natural. He told us to work quietly, so we did not disturb the animals}.",
    "text3":
        "{r: Before we could submit our report, we had to combine all the facts. My friend often had to bend his knee to look closely at the ground. He had a very good grade in school for his observations. He would always remind me to check everything twice. He had strong bones and could work for many hours. We worked together, because it was better for the team}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:We worked partially in the office and partially outside. We worked until the sun went down each day. We knew our efforts would bring a victory. When we made a mistake, our chief would remind us gently. We sometimes worked in pairs, one male and one female. This allowed us to extend our working hours without getting too tired. We hoped to finish the project before the end of the quarter}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Project's Success[/center]\nFriend: How was the new project with the new chief?\nMe: It was good! When he came, his first action was to hire new people. We had many female workers. Our daily task was interesting. We had to extend our observations as much as possible.\nFriend: And the cruelty you spoke about?\nMe: Yes, it was hard to see the bad influence of humans trying to destroy nature. We learned about our consciousness. While we were working, we tried to be careful. We had to submit many reports, and we had to combine facts often.\nFriend: Did you find any problems?\nMe: Not really. Before the last review, we found no big problems. We worked hard, until we felt tired. We even had a small victory when we found the hidden part. My knee felt tired, but it was worth it!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 95,
    "text1":
        "{r: Apparently, the river near our village is starting to pollute our fields. This fact is widely known, but some people still show ignorance. If we ignore this problem, it will threaten our future. The dirty water is a constant worry for all. If we don't fix this domestic issue now, it will get worse}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Many leaders gather in a circle to discuss the problem. If they decide quickly, they can supply clean water to everyone. They discuss what actions are appropriate. If we are familiar with the steps, we will start today. An alarm will sound if the water level goes up too fast. We need to act together, or we will fail}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our chief warns us: If someone tries to offend others by throwing waste, we must stop them. If we allow this abuse, we will feel great regret later. Our primary goal is to keep the river alive. If the river dies, our whole village will suffer. It is absolutely necessary to protect our water source}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:We will tie our efforts and work hard. If every person contributes, we will see a victory. We see many chickens and animals near the river. If they drink this dirty water, they will get sick. We must promote better ways for people to deal with their waste. If we succeed, we will destroy the old, bad habits. Our consciousness of the problem is high}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Protecting Our River[/center]\nFriend: What is the biggest problem in your village now?\nMe: Apparently, it's the river pollution. If we don't stop it, it will threaten all our animals and plants. Some people still show ignorance.\nFriend: What are you doing about it?\nMe: We gather in a circle to find appropriate solutions. If we supply clean water, the animals will stay alive. An alarm will ring if the water gets worse. We must not offend anyone, but we must stop the abuse.\nFriend: Do you think you will succeed?\nMe: Yes, if we tie our efforts and promote good habits, we will win. Our primary goal is to destroy the pollution. We know if we work together, it will be an absolutely clear victory for everyone, even the chickens!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 96,
    "text1":
        "{r:We had a big competition coming up, and the gathering was planned for the whole city. If we had more fuel, we would expand the area for the games. Our chief told us: If we didn't assess our plan well, we would end up with problems. The city leaders were influential, and their words had a big consequence}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The pollution in the river was a concern. If we fixed that problem, we would obtain clear water for a new pool. We thought: If we had more time, we could explore the cause of the pollution more deeply. My friend had a strange mental image of the river being clean again. He said: If the water was clean, he would climb the highest tree to see it clearly}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our goal was to combine all the best ideas. If we did not put our minds together, we would not predict the winner. If we had a bigger pocket of money, we would hire more experts. Our leader used a low volume of voice when he spoke about the rules. He knew: If the rules were not clear, the competition would be a mess}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I felt tired, and my lips were dry. If I had a drink, I would feel better. My friend said: If we explored the forest more, we might come across a hidden river. We had to assess our time well. If we could obtain more water, we would continue our work without worry. Our supreme aim was to finish the task}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Grand Plan[/center]\nFriend: What if we had more fuel for the competition?\nMe: If we had more fuel, we would expand the gathering area. If we did that, more people could come in. We want this to be a supreme event.\nFriend: And the pollution? What if it was gone?\nMe: If there was no pollution, we would obtain clear water for a new pool. We could even explore the new areas. If I had a bigger pocket, I'd hire more experts for this.\nFriend: What if you couldn't predict the consequences?\nMe: If we couldn't predict the consequences, we would assess every option carefully. We would combine all our mental efforts. If we didn't, we might end up failing. But if we continue, we will win."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 97,
    "text1":
        "[center]The Project's Problem[/center] \n {r: Our big project was going well, primarily because of the team's hard work. But if we had checked all the details, we wouldn't have found such a big offense in the plan. It was something that could annoy everyone involved. If we had paid more attention to the small parts, we wouldn't have had this problem. The team leader had to adopt a new way to work. If he hadn't decided to change our focus, we might have lost a lot of time. He had to interrupt others to get their attention, even if it wasn't pleasant. If he had known the risk, he would have done things differently from the start. We didn't want the project to crash. We needed to fix the plan's maintenance quickly. If we had let the issue freeze for too long, it would have been much worse. We had to struggle through extra hours of work. If we had been more careful at the start, we would have saved a lot of effort. We came to conclude that planning meant everything. We had to acknowledge our mistake and move forward}.",
    "text2":
        "[center]The Unexpected Storm[/center] \n {r: A pleasant day changed quickly. If we had watched the sky more carefully, we wouldn't have been surprised by the sudden storm. The wind made the old trees struggle, and if the maintenance team had fixed the wires last week, the power wouldn't have gone out. The dark clouds formed a huge shadow over the town. The cold air made us freeze. If the alarm hadn't sounded, many people wouldn't have known to get inside. The loud noise did interrupt our quiet afternoon. If the rain hadn't started so hard, there might have been less litter on the streets after the wind blew everything around. We hoped the storm would shift soon. The next morning, the sun was bright. We could see the damage. If we had been ready, the experience would have been less alarming. If everyone had picked up their trash, there wouldn't have been so much for the workers to clean. We had to acknowledge that we needed to prepare better for such events. We came to conclude that our familiarity with calm weather made us less careful}.",
  },
  {
    "lesson": 98,
    "text1":
        "{r:There was a big problem in our village, which often felt like a small universe. A thief, who had stolen money, made many people sad. The revenue that we could generate for our school was now lost. The rudeness of this action was against every moral rule. We knew that otherwise, if we did not capture him, he would continue to cause trouble}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The police crew, who had the main aim to protect us, started their work. There was a widow who relied on a small loan from the community. This loan was the money that the thief took. A butcher, who was a strong man, offered to help. We knew if we didn't rely on each other, we would be a fool to think we could win}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The tenant who lived in the small house by the river said he saw a shadow. He was not a coward, but he was afraid of the dark. The information that he gave was very important. He spoke about a man who somehow got in an old vehicle. The vehicle, which was very old, was a rare sight in our quiet district}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The police followed the vehicle that the tenant described. Otherwise, they would have lost the thief. They found him in a small building, which was full of old items. He had a small box full of the stolen money. The sunshine streamed in through the broken window, and it seemed to light up the truth. The thief, who was a young man, sat down quietly}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Justice in Our Universe[/center]\nFriend: So, the thief was caught? The man who stole the loan?\nMe: Yes! The police crew, who worked hard, captured him. The revenue that we lost will now be safe. It was a victory for our morals.\nFriend: And the widow who needed the money?\nMe: She can now rely on the community again. The butcher, who helped us, is a hero. No one is a fool if they help others, and no one is a coward if they speak up.\nFriend: What about the tenant?\nMe: The tenant, who saw the thief's vehicle, was key. The vehicle, which was old, led them right to him. Otherwise, the thief might have escaped into the sunshine."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 99,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our team had a new project that required a lot of effort. The money we had was sufficient for the start, but we knew we needed more. The people we hired were all capable and responsible. The goal we most desired was a victory for the whole community. This was the biggest task we had ever faced, and it required our full attention}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:It was necessary that we obtained the right tools. The support we needed was vital for our success. The place we worked at was an old building where the light was not always proper. We needed to afford new lamps. This small problem was something we had to tolerate, because the cost was high. We talked about the plan we had in mind}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We also faced a struggle with some bad habits. There was some abuse of materials that we could not ignore. We decided to adopt a new rule for everyone. Our consciousness of the waste we created was important. The new methods helped us to generate more revenue from our work. We found that the bad habits, which we saw previously, had to end}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Every person on the team wanted to contribute. The efforts we put in daily were huge. We knew we deserved to see a positive result. The materials we used were clean and safe. This was the most important thing we worked for. The victory we hoped for was getting closer. The plan we had was working well}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Team's Efforts[/center]\nFriend: How was the new project? Was it the one you desired?\nMe: Yes, it was! The task we had was huge, and it required a lot from us. The people we hired were all very capable and responsible.\nFriend: Did you have sufficient money?\nMe: The money we had was sufficient to start, but it was essential to obtain more. The place we worked at was not perfect. We needed to afford better light.\nFriend: Did you face any other problems?\nMe: We had to tolerate some old habits, but we tried to ignore the small things. We decided to adopt new rules for the abuse we saw. Our consciousness grew as we worked. We needed to generate more revenue, and we faced a struggle sometimes. But if we all contributed, we knew we deserved a victory."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 100,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our town has been experiencing an extreme heatwave for weeks, and the soil has been drying out. The local pilot has been flying over the farms to warn farmers about the danger. He says the current circumstances have been putting a huge pressure on everyone. The trees have been losing their green beauty, and their branches have been looking very weak. It's truly an alarming situation}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:This heat has also been causing an internal struggle for many. My neighbor, who has strong muscles, has been working in his garden without rest. He has been trying to relieve the dryness in his plants, but it's a tough battle. We have been seeing a lot of theft lately, as people have been taking water from private wells. This change in manner has been making everyone uneasy}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The pilot has been giving us a daily estimate of the water levels. He has been saying for days that our capacity for storing water is almost at its ultimate limit. We have been hearing his warnings quite frequently. It seems like the government has been trying to pursue new solutions, but nothing has been working yet. The situation is making some people feel crazy}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My small brother has been helping our neighbor, who has been fighting the heat for a long time. He has been carrying water, and his small muscles have been getting stronger. He accidentally slipped on the dry soil yesterday, but he wasn't hurt. He has been learning about the importance of water. We have been watching the sky, hoping for rain, but nothing has been happening}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Awaiting the Rain[/center]\nFriend: How has your town been doing with the heat?\nMe: It has been experiencing extreme heat, and the soil has been drying out. Our local pilot has been trying to warn everyone. He has been telling us our water capacity is near its ultimate limit.\nFriend: That sounds serious. Has the heat also been affecting people's behavior?\nMe: Yes. There has been some theft of water, which shows a change in manner. My neighbor, with his strong muscles, has been trying to relieve the dryness, but he has been struggling.\nFriend: And the pilot? Is he still flying?\nMe: Yes, he has been flying frequently, and he has been giving us a daily estimate. We have all been pursuing some solution, but the circumstances are difficult. It has been making some people feel crazy."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 101,
    "text1":
        "{r:Last week, we opened a new art exhibit in the city's vast hall. The crowd was unusually large. We had initially planned for a smaller space, but the interest in the art had grown so much that we had to move. Before the doors opened, we had already hung every frame carefully. We had worked all night to eliminate any dust, and the hall looked perfect}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:A stranger, who had arrived early, tried to oppose our entry fee. He had refused to pay the ten percent extra we asked for latecomers. His reply was rude. We explained that we had already announced the rules, and that the fee was for a good cause. We talked about the morality of art being free versus the cost of its creation. He had argued for a long time, but we had stood firm}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our host, Mr. Kamol, had already prepared everything. He had checked the timetable many times. The length of the speeches had been fixed precisely. He had hoped for a smooth opening, but the unexpected argument had caused a small rush outside. He had to use all his smart thinking to control the crowd. The external noise from the street had made it hard to hear the announcements}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:When the doors finally opened, the crowd filled the hall. We saw that the interest had truly matched our highest expectations. Many people had already heard about the exhibit online. We had expected a good number, but the actual attendance was unusually high. Most of the early visitors had paid the fee without a word, and they had immediately gone to see the main display}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Successful Opening[/center]\nFriend: How was the art exhibit? I heard the hall was vast.\nMe: It was! We had prepared everything well. The crowd was unusually big. We had already hung every frame on the walls the night before.\nFriend: Did you have any problems?\nMe: Yes, a stranger had tried to oppose the entry fee. He had refused to pay the ten percent extra. His reply was very direct. He had even tried to argue about the morality of art. But we had quickly managed to eliminate the problem.\nFriend: What about the timetable? Did you rush for anything?\nMe: Our host, Mr. Kamol, had ensured everything ran on time. He had been very smart about the timings. We had hoped for no external issues, and despite that one argument, the opening had perfectly matched our expectation."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 102,
    "text1":
        "[center]Tall Mountains[/center] \n {r:Our team's primary purpose was to explore the tall mountains. We knew a great discovery waited there, essential for our generation. It was a challenging journey, and our coach reminded us every day that hard work was key. We had multiple maps, but the reality of the high peaks was more difficult than any drawing. The wind made us freeze, and often, we had to struggle to move forward.One cold morning, we found a strange opening. It felt like the core of the mountain itself. Our lead scientist, a true master of earth science, believed it was a new source of energy. He said it would significantly change our world. We hoped it wasn't nonsense, but a real path to progress. He carried a small diary, writing every detail of our search. Inside the mountain, the path began to stretch far. We found strange plants and glowing rocks. There was no debt tied to this project; it was pure research. The communication device was not working properly. If we had lost contact, it would have been an alarming situation. We eliminated our fears and kept going. Suddenly, a small, bird-like creature with a single wing flew past. It was beautiful and strange. The scientist believed it was a witness to the mountain's long history. We collected seeds from unique plants and even found a wild pepper plant. We made a strong bond with the mountain, understanding its ancient secrets. When we returned, we planned a big exhibition to show our findings. Our hero team was celebrated. We proved that understanding nature is essential for a better future. The mountain had shared its gifts, and we were able to use them wisely}.",
    "text2":
        "[center]The Old Lighthouse Keeper[/center] \n {r:The old lighthouse(dengiz mayog'i) stood on a high cliff, watching over the ocean. Its purpose was essential: to guide ships and keep passengers safe. For many years, a master keeper(qo'riqchisi) had lived there, a true hero of the sea. His diary held stories of great storms and brave rescues. He was a witness to history, a quiet figure in a loud world. Life in the lighthouse was simple, but full of work. The keeper would stretch his old body every morning to climb to the top. He had multiple tasks: cleaning the huge light, checking the maintenance of the building, and fixing anything that broke. He had a strong bond with the sea, knowing its every shift and secret. He was a reliable person, always doing his duty. One winter, a terrible storm hit. The winds blew hard, making the whole tower struggle. The light, the core of the lighthouse, almost failed. If the keeper hadn't been so thoughtful, the light might have gone out. He used old parts and his long experience to keep it shining. He eliminated his own fear and focused only on the light. When the storm was finally over, the light had been on(on bu yerda yoqilgan bo'lishni anglatadi) the whole time. It was a significantly brave act. The keeper wrote in his diary about the night, but he mostly felt it was nonsense to call him a hero. He had simply done his job. The next day, a small ship appeared. It had almost crashed on the rocks. The captain said the lighthouse light was essential for their survival. He was a witness to the keeper's courage. The old keeper just smiled. His purpose was clear, and that was all that mattered}.",
  },
  {
    "lesson": 103,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our team has a big cooking competition next week. Before the event begins, we are going to practice our new recipe. I'm feeling a little uncertain about the taste. We will definitely win if we make no mistakes. As soon as I perceive any weakness in our dish, I will warn the team. My judgement on taste has to be perfect for us to succeed}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:While we are cooking, I will pour the special juice into the pot, and my friend will stir it. It's a key moment. We have been told that the taste is incredible. We must make sure there is no hole in the pot, or it will all run out. We're hoping no one finds anything disgusting in our food. We have a secret tip from an old chef that we are using}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:After we have finished cooking, we will tidy the kitchen completely. We can't leave a single mess. The judges will then accept our dish for testing. As soon as they have given their scores, we will advertise our success everywhere if we win. We have been working towards this goal for months, and we deserve it}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The judges are known to be very strict. Until they announce the winner, we will be on edge. This competition happens frequently, but the rules this year seem limited. Besides the taste, they also judge the way we present the dish. Our chances are merely good, but we still hope to make it. We will not rest until we know the result}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Chef's Challenge[/center]\nFriend: So, what are you doing before the competition starts?\nMe: Before it starts, I will check all our ingredients. I will definitely make sure the juice is fresh. I'm feeling a bit uncertain about the oven, so I will test it as soon as I arrive.\nFriend: And while you are cooking?\nMe: While we are cooking, I will pour the sauce, and my friend will stir it. We have to avoid any hole in the pot. We want it to be incredible, not disgusting.\nFriend: What about after you have finished?\nMe: After we have finished, we will tidy up completely. Then we will wait until they accept our dish. We hope they judge us well. We will advertise our new menu if we win."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 104,
    "text1":
        "{r:Last year, our team wanted to acquire a rare diamond for our new art project. Initially, we thought we could just buy it, but the owner refused to decline a higher offer from a rich man. We realized we couldn't simply pay more than him. It was a serious problem. We needed a proper plan to convince the owner to sell to us}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Our physician, Dr. Aliyev, also a part-time artist, suggested a bold experiment. He believed we could use light to expose the beauty of the diamond in a new way. He thought if we created an incredible advertisement showing this, we could achieve our goal. He had plenty of ideas, and we felt a sense of relief. He told us we could try to create a special exhibition with the diamond's image}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We worked in an old house next to a quiet lake. The main room, which felt like a huge bedroom, had solid walls, making it perfect for our experiment. We could have used a professional studio, but the lake house gave us more freedom. We spent days making the light better, trying to make the perfect light. We knew the owner could approve our idea if we did it right}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The first few tries were not good. We couldn't get the light to match the diamond's natural sparkle. We felt a sense of guilt that we had wasted so much time. The doctor reminded us that we could have given up, but that would have meant failing our ultimate goal. He warned us that the work could be long. His words helped to relieve our anxiety}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Diamond Dream[/center]\nMe: That diamond project was serious, wasn't it? We could have just bought it, but we couldn't, right?\nFriend: Exactly. The owner refused to decline. Initially, we thought we could acquire it easily. Dr. Aliyev's experiment was key. He said we could expose its beauty virtually.\nMe: I remember working in that bedroom by the lake. We could have used a studio, but that house was perfect. We had plenty of light, but we couldn't make it work at first. We felt a lot of guilt.\nFriend: Yes, but we couldn't have given up. Dr. Aliyev helped convince us. He knew we could achieve it. He even said the owner could approve if we did it properly."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 105,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our small town must be the quietest place on Earth. You can't hear a single loud noise here after dark. The clean air must bring great pleasure to the residents, and their general welfare must be high. I assure you, city life can't compare to this. We must organize a small festival soon to greet our new neighbors. It must be the perfect way to welcome them}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:There's been a strange incident at the old mill. Someone must have tried to dig around its foundation. This can't be a simple joke; it looks like a serious attempt to find something. My perception is that they must have been looking for an old treasure, but that can't be true. We must investigate this, and we must chase after any clues we find}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The old gate of the mill has been locked for years, but now it's open. Someone must have found a way to unlock it. We can't allow just anyone to enter the property. There's a strong fear that valuable old things could be stolen. I heard a quiet whisper in the wind last night, almost like a warning. We must replace the lock immediately; it can't be safe like this}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My grandmother, who lives near the mill, has a great dislike for unnecessary activity there. She must have seen something, but she won't say. She must be worried. Every autumn, she must harvest her garden before the cold weather starts. She also must sweep her bathroom daily, and she must mop the kitchen floor every morning. She can't tolerate any mess}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Mill Mystery[/center]\nMe: That noise at the mill last night. It must have been someone trying to unlock the gate.\nFriend: Yes, they must have. My perception is that they can't be good people. They must have been looking for something specific. It can't be a joke, that's for sure(for sure aniq degani).\nMe: No. We must dig into this. We can't just ignore it. There's a fear in the town about it. My grandmother has a strong dislike for such things.\nFriend: I assure you, we must chase down them. We can't allow this to become a big problem. We must organize a proper investigation, and then we can define what happened."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 106,
    "text1":
        "{r:There’s a strange crack in the old mirror in our household. It might have appeared last night. My mother is upset; she says it must be a bad sign. I wonder what could have caused it. The cat may have jumped onto the shelf, or a picture might have fallen. It can't have been a simple accident; the crack is very deep. We must find out the reason for it soon}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:My brother says the old mirror might have been an asset to the house, but now it is broken. He thinks someone may have tried to reverse its position or specifically moved it. He says he doesn't disagree that it is a bad sign, but he doesn't believe it is a ghost. We must honor the old things in the house, and we must be careful with them. This incident is a test of our care}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We may have forgotten to close the window, and the wind might have caused the crack. It is a contemporary idea that even small things can cause big problems. The tiny flowers outside might have bloomed earlier this year, and their smell may have filled the room. I barely remember seeing the window open. I pray it was just the wind, nothing more serious. We must remember to wrap the mirror to prevent more damage}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My father says the priority is to fix the mirror. He says it might have been a sign for us to advance our efforts in keeping the house safe. His words make me think. This whole thing may have been a wake-up call for us to be more careful. Our family has an achievement of keeping this house safe for generations. We must continue this tradition forever}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Mysterious Mirror[/center]\nMe: The mirror cracked! What might have caused it?\nFriend: Hmm, it may have been the cat. It might have jumped onto the shelf. Or the old wood may have cracked because it is very old.\nMe: I don't know. My brother says it might have been someone trying to reverse its position. He doesn't disagree with the bad sign, but he says it can't be a ghost. He says it must be an asset that we must honor.\nFriend: We can't know for sure. Someone may have forgotten to lock the window, and the wind might have done it. We must wrap it properly now. What's the priority?\nMe: The priority is to get a permit to replace it. We must also request a new display area for it. It can't remain broken forever."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 107,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our small museum has a new schedule for visitors. Everyone mustn't touch the old artifacts; that's the first rule to preserve them. You don't need to pay an entry fee if you have our special membership. We have made sure to get approval from the city council for these new rules. It's extremely important that everyone follows them. We're hoping to transform the visitor experience}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:There was a sudden scream from the ancient art section this morning. A guard ran to the scene. He saw a man trying to drag a statue. The man mustn't have known the guard was there. The guard was unable to catch him easily, but he managed to give a brief warning. The police now have a suspect, and an arrest might be made soon. They needn't have caused such a problem; they could have just asked for permission to watch}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The police said that the old documents in the archive mustn't fade any more. We don't need to use flash cameras near them. Over time, these documents evolve and become more fragile. They shrink slightly with age. It's a slow process, but it is happening. The experts said we must add a new protective layer of glass to their display to preserve them for future generations}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:For the new display, we made a special purchase of steel supports. The expense was high, but it was essential. My colleague said, 'We needn't have bought such strong supports; lighter ones would have worked.' But I disagree; we must ensure maximum safety. We found an old coin near the statue; it mustn't be touched until the police finish their investigation. We don't need to clean it yet}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Museum Rules[/center]\nMe: We mustn't forget to greet the new visitors with a smile! And they mustn't touch anything.\nFriend: Right. We don't need to remind them about every rule if they read the sign. What about that scream from the mill? The suspect must have tried to drag something out.\nMe: Yes, the police said an arrest might happen soon. They needn't have tried to steal; it was extremely foolish. The old documents mustn't fade further, so we don't need to expose them to bright light.\nFriend: And the steel supports for the new display? We needn't have spent so much money on them, did we?\nMe: I think we must be careful about the expense. We must preserve these items. It can't be too much. It's for the approval of everyone."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 108,
    "text1":
        "{r:Looking back at my childhood days, I should have spent more time playing outside, not always reading. My parents shouldn't have let me abandon my musical instruments so easily; now I regret it. We lived in a small settlement near the lake, and I should have explored it more. I shouldn't have let small failures discourage me from trying new things. Now, I suppose, it's too late for some of those things}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:For tomorrow's cooking class, I should memorize all the ingredients. We shouldn't skip any steps; the teacher will evaluate us strictly. I should bake the bread for exactly 30 minutes. My friend says I should spin the dough before baking to get a good result. I shouldn't doubt myself, but sometimes the pressure is high. I should try to make the bread sparkle with a little butter on top}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:After the class, the applause must have been for someone else, not me. I saw the teacher frown, and I heard a sigh. I shouldn't have added so much pepper to the soup; it was too strong. I should have tasted it more carefully. Someone tried to whistle as a joke, but it didn't help my mood. My friend said I shouldn't take it so seriously, but it was important to me}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My current earnings are quite low. I should edit my resume and find a better job. I shouldn't occupy my time with unimportant tasks. I should also double check my finances before making any large purchase. I should have started saving earlier, but I didn't. Now, it is a challenge to manage everything. I must take more responsibility for my future}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Lessons Learned[/center]\nMe: I should have studied harder for that exam. I really regret it now.\nFriend: You're right, you should have. We all should evaluate our efforts more often. I shouldn't have let that small failure discourage me in my childhood.\nMe: And for this cooking class tomorrow, what should we do?\nFriend: We should memorize all the steps for baking. We shouldn't skip anything. We should aim for the applause.\nMe: I suppose we should edit our recipe one last time. I shouldn't frown if it doesn't sparkle perfectly. It is just a class, after all. We should try to enjoy it."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 109,
    "text1":
        "{r:It's time for me to take some initiative and change my occupation. My current work is causing my stress to reduce, but it's not giving me enough pleasure. I'd better start looking for a new job immediately, or I'll never find something better. Also I have to talk to my landlord about the rent increase. It's time we had a serious conversation about it, because it's getting too expensive}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Before we start our mountain hike, it's time to wear our helmets. It's advisable that everyone checks their equipment. We'd better not take any risks; the path can be dangerous, and we can't afford any faults. The park rangers gave us a notice about the changing weather. We'd better descend before the storm hits, or we might get stuck. It's vital that we follow the warning}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My friend, Alex, seemed to be in a strange mood all morning. I saw a shiver run through him when I mentioned the old house. I'd better ask him what's wrong. It's time he told me. Perhaps he needs to confess something. I suppose it's a small problem, but it's affecting his behavior. I could write him a note with ink if he can't talk to me directly. I'd better prepare a safe space for him to speak}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:It's high time the team leaders announced the definition of our new project goals. We'd better all be on the same page. It's vital for our success. We must also reduce any unnecessary expenses. Everyone had better focus on the priority tasks now. Our team manager said it's time we showed some real progress. After the meeting, I think a comforting hug might be needed for some of the younger members}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Making Decisions[/center]\nMe: It's time I talked to my landlord about the rent. It's getting too high.\nFriend: You'd better do that soon. It's vital to fix that problem.\nMe: And for our hike tomorrow, it's time to get our helmets. We'd better not forget them.\nFriend: Right. We must reduce any risks. What about Alex's strange mood? It's time he told us what's on his mind. He must confess something.\nMe: I agree. I'd better talk to him. And for the project, it's high time they announced a clear definition. We all need to take initiative.\nFriend: Exactly. We'd better all be ready for the challenge."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 110,
    "text1":
        "{r:Growing up, my grandmother would always tell me stories about a hidden mine full of resources near our village. I would spend hours imagining the overall wealth it would bring. It would be an incredible achievement for our community. I often thought I would find it one day. My niece, who has a strong similarity to me in her dreams, would also love to discover such a place. It would change our existence forever}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Last week, we got stuck in a difficult situation. My friend made a huge error during our school project. I would have helped him earlier, but he didn't ask. He wouldn't admit his mistake, and that would only make things worse. I thought he would confess it, but he didn't. We must be consistent in our honesty. I said to him, 'You should have told us before,' and he gave a small sigh}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I wouldn't forgive someone who would betray my trust. A formal apology wouldn't even be enough. I would feel a deep dislike. My old teacher would always say, 'You shouldn't scratch old wounds.' I suppose he would be right. My niece would never betray anyone; she is extremely loyal. I would always back her up}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:At our family gatherings, my uncle would always clap his hands and start a joke. He would often roast the chicken perfectly, and we would all enjoy the great food. Sometimes, he would flip a coin to decide who would do the dishes. He wouldn't accept any excuses. This would always be followed by lots of laughter and applause. His presence would always make the mood light}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]What Would Happen?[/center]\nMe: If you had the chance, what would you do?\nFriend: I would find that hidden mine my grandmother would talk about. It would be an incredible discovery.\nMe: That would be amazing! I wouldn't betray anyone's trust to get there. What about your friend who made the error?\nFriend: He wouldn't listen to my advice. I would have helped him, but he didn't ask. He should have told us. It was a silly mistake.\nMe: True. He shouldn't have done that. Our family wouldn't forgive such a betrayal easily. Overall, honesty is vital}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 111,
    "text1":
        "{r:We had to move the bulk of the old furniture today. It was a huge task, and I knew I couldn't do it alone. I asked my friend, 'Can you help me drag these heavy boxes?' He said, 'Of course! We can't let you do this by yourself.' There was a time constraint, so we had better work fast. I was so glad he could accompany me. It must have taken us hours}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Later, we had a small disagreement about the best way to organize the new room. I asked, 'Would you mind listening to my idea for a minute?' He said, 'I suppose so, but your ideas are often too complicated.' I tried to elaborate on my plan, but he seemed to resist it. I felt a slight rejection. 'Could you please give it a proper chance?' I asked. He just gave a small frown and said nothing}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We heard that the new palace display is open to the public tomorrow. 'Would you like to go with me?' I asked. 'I could even drive,' I added. He said, 'That would be nice. What time should we meet?' It is a noticeable change from his earlier mood. I suppose he must have forgotten our small disagreement. 'Can I offer to bring some drinks?' I asked. He smiled. This might just turn out to be a fun day}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:We're still dealing with the garbage from the move. I saw a few old cans. 'Can I crush these metal cans for you?' I asked my brother. He said, 'Sure, but be careful. You shouldn't stumble on that loose board.' The number of cans seems to multiply every day. I wonder if we should find a new place to put the recycling, elsewhere in the garden. We don't need to keep it all here}.",
  },
  {
    "lesson": 112,
    "text1":
        "{r:I wish I had more time to relax. The overall stress at work has increased considerably, and I'm feeling extremely exhausted. I wish my boss wouldn't give us so much extra work. I also wish the office would become a bit more neat; it is always a mess. It would be a great relief if I could just spend a day doing nothing. I wish I had taken a proper break last month}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:There was a strange event that occurred at the annual dinner. The main dish, a large turkey, simply vanished. I wish I hadn't been the one to bring it. The chef made an announcement that he would replace it, but the mood was already strange. I wish we could find the offender. My uncle said he wishes people wouldn't steal food, it's brutal. It was a noticeable problem that ruined the evening}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I wish I hadn't been so quick to judge the new regulations. Now I understand their valid points. It is imperative that we remove any old laws that forbid progress. I wish the community would opt for more modern ideas. The current rules are as fragile as an old tale now. I wish I could convince everyone that change is essential. It would be a great achievement}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My sister said she wishes her friends wouldn't betray her trust so easily. She had a very distinct disagreement with one of them. She wishes she hadn't shared her secret with them. Her face showed a clear frown. I wish I could give her more comfort. She wishes they would be more gentle with her feelings. It's a difficult time for her, and I wish I could take her pain away}.",
  },
  {
    "lesson": 113,
    "text1":
        "{r:News of the new energy pill was broadcast last night. It is alleged that this pill can transform anyone into a superior human, capable of incredible feats. However, there is a lot of resistance from some doctors. I don't like being told what to believe so easily. This pill is supposedly a magic solution, but I feel an urge to examine it more closely. It must be analyzed before it is given to the public}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:In the forest nearby, a rare insect was recently discovered. It is thought to be an inferior version of a known species, but its unique features are noticeable. It doesn't like being chased or observed closely. This insect gets hunted by a small bird, a predator that would soar high above the trees. The bird would then descend rapidly to catch its prey. It's a brutal dance of existence}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:A new water pump was manufactured last week, and it is being tested today. It is said to be so powerful it can squeeze water from almost any source. I was born in this dry region, and I wish we had such a pump when I was a child. We would have had plenty of water. A subtle hum was heard as the pump was turned on, and an echo of its power filled the valley. It is a truly impressive piece of technology}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:A bag of candy was offered to the children at the park. They were given specific instructions: 'You mustn't eat all of it at once.' However, the candy was quickly consumed. I don't like being lectured about my diet, but sometimes it is necessary. I wish I hadn't eaten so much candy yesterday; now I feel unwell. My friend said he was given a brief warning about the sugar, but he didn't listen}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The New Invention[/center]\nMe: The new energy pill has caused a lot of resistance. I don't like being told that it's a magic solution.\nFriend: I agree. It is alleged to make people superior, but it might be dangerous. What about that new water pump? It was manufactured quickly.\nMe: Yes, and it is supposedly able to squeeze water from almost anything. I was born in a dry area, so I wish we had that pump then. I also heard a rare insect was discovered nearby. It gets hunted by a predator that would soar very high.\nFriend: Interesting. Could I ask you: Do you think there is a subtle connection between these events?\nMe: Perhaps. There's an urge to negotiate for more information. We must find the answers.",
  },
  {
    "lesson": 114,
    "text1":
        "{r:It is said that many years ago, a great peasant revolt occurred in this region. The leader of the revolt is said to have been a former hunter, known for his courage in combat. He was supposedly a magician too, able to survive attacks that would have killed anyone else. It is believed that his aim was to end the brutal punishment imposed by the old ruler. The old stories still echo in these lands}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Today, we are supposed to receive a new delivery of flour for the bakery. The local authorities recently issued a ban on certain types of meat, specifically beef, due to a health warning. This removal of beef from menus is supposed to reduce certain health risks. It is said that the new rules will accelerate our shift towards healthier diets. We are also not supposed to use any pig products in our cookies anymore}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The mayor is expected to announce new plans for the city's old market. It is said that the market's layout will curve in a different direction to allow for more space. The council is supposed to resume their meetings next week to discuss the details. However, some members are said to hesitate about the new design. It is hoped that the project will accelerate quickly once approval is given}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My brother was supposed to tidy up his closet yesterday, but he didn't. His clothes are still in a messy fold on the floor. It is said that a messy room leads to a messy mind. He is supposed to confess when he makes a mistake, but he often resists. I wish he would just do what he is supposed to do. I'd better remind him later. He must take more responsibility for his space}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Old Village and New Rules[/center]\nMe: It is said that the old peasant revolt here was led by a magician.\nFriend: Really? He is said to have had incredible powers in combat. I suppose he was supposed to be a great hero.\nMe: Yes. Anyway, what are we supposed to do about the new ban on beef and pig products?\nFriend: We are not supposed to use them in the bakery anymore. It is said that this removal will accelerate health benefits. The new delivery of flour is also supposed to arrive today.\nMe: Right. And my brother is supposed to confess about his messy closet. I wish he wouldn't hesitate so much."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 115,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our small village decided to renew the old temple. It had to be done by experts, so we had the roof repaired and the walls painted. It was part of a larger expansion project. A longtime companion of the mayor was given the privilege of controlling the work. There was a strange rumor going around that the temple had a secret passage, but it was never proven. We had to implement a strict schedule}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Suddenly, an unexpected frost hit the fields, and the ground turned to mud. One of our cows got stuck and almost drowned in the mud. We had to get the mud drained quickly, but it was a huge task. There was an allegation that someone had deliberately damaged the farm's drainage system. The police said a sentence could be given if the offender was found. I hope they don't hesitate to punish them}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Because of the frost damage, we had to make a shift in our farm's schedule. We had some special coverings made to restrict further damage to the crops. My uncle said, 'We should get the large tarpaulin installed properly.' A strong wind threatened to rip it, so we had to work fast. We don't need to soak the ground too much; it's already full of water. This was a problem we should have foreseen}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:My grandmother had her old dress renewed for the upcoming festival. She had the delicate lace repaired and the fabric cleaned. It was a privilege to wear such an old dress. She also had her hair styled at the new salon. She said, 'I had my hair cut short; it's a pleasant change.' She would often talk about having things done for her. She used to get her shoes polished every week}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Community Challenges[/center]\nMe: The temple looks beautiful now. We had its roof renewed just in time.\nFriend: Yes, and the expansion is going well. We had the new walls built very quickly. Did you hear about the allegation about the farm's drainage system?\nMe: Yes, it is said someone damaged it. That poor cow almost drowned in the mud. They had to get the drainage fixed immediately.\nFriend: I know. The frost caused a huge problem. We also had to get the covers installed to restrict further damage. It was quite a shift in our daily plans.\nMe: Definitely. It just shows you never know what you will have happen to you. I wish we could implement a way to prevent these things."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 116,
    "text1":
        "{r:Last night, my friend called me, feeling overwhelmed. He said that the rain was worsening and that a major flood was coming. He told me that it was like a nightmare for him. He said that the water would persist and rise throughout the night. I wished I could do more to help him, but he was a long way away. It was a truly brutal situation}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The next morning, a local news report stated that an old cave near the river had collapsed. It was reported that the constant pressure of the flood had caused its walls to weaken. The police said that they were investigating a rumor of fraud related to the cave's construction. They told the public that the motive for the fraud was unclear, but they were consistently seeking answers. It was said that a farmer's bull had been near the cave just before the collapse}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My aunt, who lives near the river, called me, her voice full of fear. She said that she had started to tremble when she heard the news. She told me that the sound of the collapsing cave was still echoing in her mind. She said that she couldn't swallow her food because of the anxiety. She wished the memories would soften with time. She also said that the flood had been a terrible burden on the whole village}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Our community leader held an emergency meeting. He told us that he was going to motivate everyone to clean up the damage. He said that they would facilitate the removal of mud and debris from the basements. He explained that special pumps would be used to suck the water out. He said that we should all work together to restore the area. He also stressed that we should not hesitate to ask for help}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]After the Flood[/center]\nMe: I just talked to your aunt. She said that she was still trembling from the flood.\nFriend: I know. She told me she couldn't swallow anything. She said the memory would persist for a long time. She wishes it would soften.\nMe: The community leader said that he was going to motivate everyone for the clean-up. He told us that they would facilitate clearing the basements.\nFriend: That's good. He said they would suck all the water out. It is such a burden on everyone. And the news reported that the cave had weakened due to the flood.\nMe: Yes, and they are investigating a fraud. They said the motive was still unknown. It is a real nightmare. I hope they find the offender. That poor bull was near the cave, too."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 117,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our village has always faced a strange restriction on the number of sheep we can raise. I often wonder why this rule exists. My grandmother once told me that it was for our survival, but she didn't explain further. I wish I knew what the real reason was. I asked the elder if he knew why the restriction was applied. He only sighed and said that sometimes, we must simply endure without understanding. I still feel a certain curiosity}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The trial of the alleged fraudulent merchant began yesterday. The judge asked the prosecutor if he had enough evidence to convict the man. He also wanted to know what the motive for the fraud was. The merchant was said to be as strong as a warrior, but he looked pale. It was reported that a lot of illegal garbage had been found near his pond. The police asked him if he was guilty of illegally dumping waste. He wouldn't answer them}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I wanted to understand the true story behind the restriction. I wondered if the naked truth would ever be revealed. I asked the old storyteller if he could tell me more. He said that some things were hidden behind a curtain of time. He explained that sometimes, old laws persist because people are afraid to modify them. He also told me that it took great persistence to uncover ancient secrets. I hoped I had courage to continue searching}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The community elders called an emergency meeting to discuss the rising crime rate. They asked what could be done to prevent harm. It was said that a simultaneous rise in fraudulent activities had been observed. They wanted to know if the new police chief would implement stricter laws. My uncle asked if they could put more resources into the local security forces. He also suggested that we should have a supply of cotton bandages ready for any emergency}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Hidden Truth[/center]\nMe: I wonder why there's such a restriction on our sheep.\nFriend: Me too. I asked the elder if he knew the reason. He just said we had to endure it.\nMe: It's like the fraudulent merchant's trial. I wanted to know if he was guilty of dumping garbage near the pond. The judge asked the prosecutor if he had enough evidence to convict him. He looks like a tired warrior.\nFriend: Yeah. I also wondered if the naked truth about that old restriction would ever be revealed. I asked the storyteller if he could tell me more. He said it took persistence.\nMe: I agree. And it's like the simultaneous rise in crime. The elders asked what could be done to prevent harm. They also wanted to know if the new police would modify anything. They suggested we should get more cotton for first aid."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 118,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our team leader said he was going to motivate us. He believes that even a small particle of effort can boost our overall performance. I think so too. He told us that we shouldn't let negative rumors undermine our confidence. We had a very complex task ahead, and he hoped we would all unite to achieve it. He also asked, 'Are you feeling overwhelmed?' 'No, I'm not,' I replied. 'Neither am I,' said my companion}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:We had to spend a night in the wilderness after our car broke down. It was a weird experience. The cold was intense, and I began to sweat from fear. I asked, 'Do you think we will survive?' My friend replied, 'I hope so. We have to.' We couldn't find a safe cave, and the darkness was endless. The silence was only broken by the occasional sound of a bat flying by. It was a truly brutal test of our endurance}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The detective was investigating a strange case involving stolen possessions. He said it was a very complex situation, full of unexpected twists. He asked the witness, 'Do you think the man was drunken when he committed the crime?' The witness replied, 'I don't think so. He seemed quite sober.' The detective then said that the motive was still a mystery. He told us that he was sure he would find the truth. We hoped so too}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The poet's words had a profound impact on me. He managed to convey such deep feelings with every particle of his speech. I asked my literature teacher, 'Does he always write like that?' She replied, 'Oh, he does! He's a true genius.' He received much praise for his work. It is said that his poems can even soften the hardest hearts. I think so. He is expected to publish a new collection soon}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Unfolding Mystery[/center]\nMe: Our leader said he could boost our spirit. Do you think so?\nFriend: I hope so. We need it. This whole situation is so complex, and the rumors try to undermine our efforts. I asked him, 'Are we going to unite all the resources?' He said he thought so.\nMe: I hope we can survive in this wilderness a bit longer. It was a weird night.\nFriend: Neither did I enjoy it. The endless darkness made me sweat. That bat flying around was strange, too.\nMe: And what about the stolen possessions? The detective said he thought the case was full of twists. He asked if we thought the person was drunken. I don't think so.\nFriend: Neither do I. But his words convey a profound truth. I hope they will find the thief. I think they will."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 119,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our company's profits began to decline sharply. We had to make a huge effort to find new solutions. I didn't mind working extra hours to help. My manager decided to implement a new strategy. He suggested analyzing all our past data simultaneously. It was a test of our collective endurance. We couldn't afford to fail now}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:There was a strange silence during the board meeting. Some members seemed to pretend to be calm, but their tension was genuine. I felt something was wrong. Later, we discovered a rumor that someone was trying to conduct a leak of confidential information. It made me mad to think that anyone would betray our trust. We had to find the offender}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The new security system was complex. I had to learn to press a specific button and then tighten a dial simultaneously. It took some effort. I noticed a loose wire near the old dustbin that needed fixing. Before leaving for the day, I made sure to report it. No one would dare to ignore such a small, but potentially dangerous, detail. We always aim to keep things neat}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I was truly grateful to receive the award for my work. My grandmother said she was proud of me. She always told me not to be mean or rude to anyone. Her words came from a distant memory of her own youth. She remembered struggling to survive during difficult times. I enjoy listening to her tales of the past; they are always so profound}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Office Challenges[/center]\nMe: Our profits continue to decline. I suggested making a huge effort.\nFriend: I agree. We can't afford to lose more money. It's a real test of our endurance. Are you ready to face the challenge?\nMe: Yes, I am. I don't mind staying in workplace until night to work on it. Simultaneously, there's that rumor about someone trying to conduct a leak. It makes me mad.\nFriend: I know. Some people seem to pretend to be innocent, but I feel their guilt. There's a strange silence about it. We'd better not ignore it.\nMe: Definitely. Overall, did you manage to fix that loose wire near the dustbin?\nFriend: Oh, yes! I remembered to press the button and tighten it before leaving. I'm grateful to have a safe place to work."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 120,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our team has been given a new project this month, a significant responsibility. We would like to dedicate ourselves completely to this project. I wouldn't mind staying late to ensure its success. My colleague said he would prefer to finish everything before the deadline. We all would hate to disappoint the manager. It's a very delicate task that requires our full attention}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The detective was investigating a strange case. He would like to know more about the suspect. He asked, 'Would you mind telling me if the witness was frozen with fear?' The witness said that she had felt a cold hook in her stomach. She would hate to betray anyone, but she felt a necessity to tell the truth. The suspect's strange tattoos on his forehead only added to the mystery}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My neighbor's dog would bark loudly every morning. I wouldn't mind it if it wasn't so early. I would prefer to sleep a bit longer. I tried to talk to my neighbor, but he seemed to be a rebel who didn't care about anyone else. I wished I could just suspend the noise. My spouse said he would love to help me find a solution, but he didn't know what to do}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I was preparing for a very delicate cooking competition. I would like to win it. I practiced using a special fork for the pastry. The instructions said that each step had to be precise. I would hate to make a mistake. My coach said, 'Would you mind reviewing the recipe one more time?' I didn't mind doing so; it was my privilege to learn from him. I hoped I would not be frozen with fear on the day of the competition}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Daily Decisions[/center]\nMe: I would like to dedicate more time to my hobbies this year. How about you?\nFriend: I would love to travel more. I would also prefer to avoid loud noises. My neighbor's dog would bark all the time. I wouldn't mind him barking if it wasn't so early.\nMe: I know! He's a real rebel. And I would hate to have such a noisy problem in our neighborhood. Did you hear about the police case?\nFriend: Yes. The detective asked if I would mind telling him what I had seen. He also mentioned something about a frozen suspect.\nMe: It sounds complex. I would prefer to stay out of it. Did you see that strange hook on the suspect's forehead?\nFriend: I did! And that delicate carving. What a mystery! My spouse would hate to live near such a person."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 121,
    "text1":
        "{r:After the power outage, I had a choice: crawl up the stairs or wait for the elevator. I prefer to take the elevator rather than crawl, but it was frozen. The anxiety of being stuck was always mild for me, but some people were truly mad. It was almost noon, and we needed a precise solution. I would prefer to wait for the repair crew, but some of my colleagues were starting to panic. We were altogether in a tricky situation}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:My niece brought her favorite doll to me. She said she would rather I didn't carve anything on it, but just fix its loose ankle. I promised to be very cautious. I prefer to work with small tools, like a needle, for such delicate repairs. I would rather she was patient, as this would take time. She gave me a hint of her bold plan for the doll's new look, which was almost a madness for a toy, but I didn't say anything}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Our coach told us, 'I would rather you pushed yourselves harder than you hesitated.' He would hate to see us give up. When I felt the anxiety in my belly, I would rather focus on my breathing. He said he would prefer us to fight with a closed fist of determination. He emphasized that a mild effort wasn't enough. He would rather we showed our true dedication altogether}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I had a big decision to make about my future studies. I would prefer to enroll in a program that allowed me to travel. I would rather endorse a plan that gives me more freedom. My parents prefer me to study closer to home, but I feel a strong desire for a more distant education. It's a precise choice that requires careful thought. I don't want to regret anything}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Making Choices[/center]\nMe: I would rather take the elevator than crawl up the stairs. This anxiety is getting to me.\nFriend: I know. I prefer to wait for the repairs. It's already past noon. I would rather they fixed it soon. This whole situation is a kind of madness.\nMe: True. And I would rather you didn't hint at my bold ideas, especially about trying to carve on that doll.\nFriend: Don't worry, I won't. I would hate to upset your niece. I prefer to help her with a small needle for her doll's ankle. It's a delicate job.\nMe: Thanks. I would prefer to enroll in that new art class altogether. I would rather dedicate my time to something creative than just work. My fist is ready to grab that opportunity!\nFriend: I endorse that idea! You deserve it. And I would rather you were happy than stressed. Just be cautious."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 122,
    "text1":
        "{r:Moving to the new city was a huge shift. At first, I was reluctant to leave my old life, and everything felt so alien. I had to get used to the constant noise and the fast pace. It took a while to blend in with the local culture. My teenager cousin, however, seemed to embrace the change quickly. He was used to a lot of liberty back home, so the new freedoms here didn't scare him. I think he will get used to it very quickly}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The magnitude of the challenge was enormous. Our funds began to diminish, and it became a necessity to find new investors. We entered a tough negotiation, and my boss was always cautious, trying to avoid any bias. He said we couldn't afford to cancel the project. He had been used to working under pressure for years, but even he admitted this was hard. We had to get used to the idea that success wasn't guaranteed, and some of our initial plans might vanish}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I used to eat a lot of fast food, but now I am used to preparing my own decent meals. It was hard to get used to peeling so many vegetables every day. I also used to stay up late, but now I am used to going to bed at precisely ten o'clock. My doctor said that my old habits were harmful, and I realized he was right. I don't want to scare myself with bad health again}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Our next destination was a country known for its beautiful silk production. The cultural differences were vast. At first, I was reluctant to try some of the local dishes. The smell would scare me. I had to get used to eating food I wasn't familiar with. Some tourists even started a small rebellion against the local customs, but I think it's a necessity to be respectful. I am now used to seeing people dressed in silk everywhere, and I find it quite beautiful}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Adapting to Change[/center]\nMe: It took me a while to get used to living in this city. Everything felt so alien.\nFriend: Excellent, you finally got used to it! I used to think I'd never get used to the magnitude of the crowds. But now, I am used to it. I enjoy the liberty of anonymity.\nMe: True. And the negotiations at work can be tough. I used to avoid them, but now I am used to handling them. You just have to be cautious.\nFriend: That's a good point. I also had to get used to peeling all those vegetables for dinner. I used to hate it!\nMe: Haha! And our new destination for vacation... I hope I can get used to the hot weather. I don't want it to diminish my enjoyment. I also hope we don't have to cancel anything, but I think it's a necessity to be ready for anything."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 123,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our neighborhood decided against letting the old oak tree on the lawn be cut down. We all insisted on preserving it, as it was a precious landmark. I succeeded in organizing a petition. The council initially wanted to prohibit any gatherings near it, but we convinced them otherwise. Our team felt like celebrating this outstanding victory. It was as if an angel had helped us}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The trial was tense. The defendant was accused of giving false testimony. He insisted on telling his story, and he would swear on his family's honor that he was innocent. The prosecutor's arguments seemed to be heavily biased towards a conviction. The judge prevented the defense lawyer from asking a crucial question, which raised some concerns. We hoped to find some precious new evidence soon to clear his name}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The coastal town was preparing for a strong storm. The police issued a warning, saying it would prohibit anyone from approaching the beach. The tide was rising rapidly, and the magnitude of the waves was alarming. They installed artificial barriers to stop the water from reaching the houses. We all thought of helping where we could. It was a matter of necessity}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:After the concert, the audience began to applaud the outstanding performance. Everyone congratulated the singer on delivering such a moving show. She thanked us for being there and for our support. She had asked for permission to play an extra song, and the crowd cheered. She seemed like an angel on stage, her voice was so pure. I looked forward to seeing her perform again soon}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Community & Conviction[/center]\nMe: I'm so glad we succeeded in saving the oak tree on the lawn!\nFriend: Me too! That was excellent! I thought of giving up at one point, but everyone insisted on fighting for it. It was truly outstanding.\nMe: Definitely! Did you hear about that trial? They accused the defendant of giving false evidence. I hope they won't prohibit him from seeing his family.\nFriend: Yes. The judge's decisions seemed a bit biased. I heard the defendant swore on his life he was innocent. It's a precious right to be heard.\nMe: It is. I just wish they could stop the tide of negative opinions from rising. Anyway, I'm looking forward to seeing you at the community appreciation dinner. We can thank the organizers for getting us permission to use the hall. It's a truly artificial setting, but it will be fun!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 124,
    "text1":
        "{r:There has been a severe shortage of water lately in our small village. It's no use complaining about it, but we need a solution. Our elder, a true genius, proposed a plan to oversee the distribution. He insisted on making a sacrifice for the common good. We are a loyal tribe, and we wouldn't mind contributing our effort. It's worth trying anything to prevent a crisis}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The rumor about the new dam was ridiculous. There's no point in believing such false claims. The mayor had difficulty making it credible to the public. He didn't like being contradicted. One journalist insisted on publishing a story that wasn't verified, and the mayor felt like giving him a slap. It was a moment that made everyone's jaw drop. It felt like a total waste of time trying to negotiate with him}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I was very busy preparing for my upcoming exam. It wasn't worth wasting any time on distractions. My old friend suggested going out, but I decided against doing so. There was no point in risking my future. I had to study hard, and I spent hours reviewing my notes. The cancellation of my weekend plans was a small sacrifice compared to the magnitude of this exam}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Our new mentor would inspire us with his dedication. He had difficulty explaining complex theories, but he never gave up. He believed it was worth making an effort to help everyone. He found a loyal mate in our team who would help him oversee the progress. He spent a lot of time listening to our concerns. We all felt a strong connection to him, almost like a tribe}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Unforeseen Crisis[/center]\nMe: This shortage of food lately is ridiculous. It's no use complaining.\nFriend: I agree. And there's no point in blaming anyone now. We need a genius to inspire us.\nMe: I think so too. That is a cool idea! Our leader is busy trying to oversee the distribution, but he has difficulty finding a credible solution.\nFriend: It's not worth getting mad about it, but I feel like giving that false genius a slap on the jaw for his lies! He caused all this panic!\nMe: Haha, I understand the feeling! We spent hours listening to his nonsense. It was a waste of time trying to reason with him. We just need to be loyal to our tribe and make this sacrifice together."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 125,
    "text1":
        "{r:The ancient kingdom prepared for a grand festival. The queen planned to make a public appearance, so that her people could feel her presence. Her bodyguard stood a short distance away, his hand near his sword, ready to tackle any threat. This festival was for the glory of the kingdom, and they wanted it to be perfect. Thorough preparations were underway for both outdoor and indoor events}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:A wealthy merchant arrived in the city, bringing a strange mystery with him. He came to donate a large sum of money to the local orphanage. He said it was for a good reason. People tried to understand his motives, so that they could figure out his secret. He wouldn't say much, but sometimes he would bow his head, as if in deep thought. His story was still a bubble of speculation}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The new prison inmate was assigned a simple task: to brush the old concrete walls. This brush was for cleaning tough stains. He worked diligently, so that he could prove his dedication and gain early release. He preferred to focus on his work rather than think about his past. He hoped the guards would endorse his effort}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I met my old buddy at the outdoor market. He was there to buy fresh fruit. He pointed to a pile of ripe peaches. 'These are for making my grandma's famous pie,' he said. He needed a lot, so that he could make enough for the whole family. We talked for a while, sharing stories from our youth. We decided to have dinner together then}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]The Royal Visit[/center]\nMe: The queen's bodyguard is very cautious. He stands at a safe distance.\nFriend: Yes, he does. He's there to protect her, so that she can greet her people safely. This entire festival is for the glory of the kingdom.\nMe: True. And the merchant who donated money... he also brought a sword to display. It's an outstanding piece of art.\nFriend: Indeed. I heard he came to clear up a mystery. He's also going to brush some old documents for the royal library.\nMe: Interesting. I wonder if he will bow to the queen when she arrives. I think he will. The concrete path is ready for her arrival, and the peaches are ready for eating at the indoor festival. Everything is thorough to the last detail!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 126,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our homeland was under a new threat. A hostile group had taken our people hostage. We were afraid to act quickly, as it could ruin everything. No one was interested in starting a rebellion without a clear plan. We were afraid of losing more lives. The whole situation felt like a cage, trapping us. The news spread instantly, and the magnitude of the crisis was spectacular, but in a terrifying way}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The leader stood firm. He would never let his people live in fear. He spoke with inspiration, and we felt an increase of loyalty. 'I'm sorry to say this, but we cannot allow this hostile group to state their dominance here,' he declared. 'We must take a measure instantly!' I was interested to know his strategy. Afterward, we all prepared for the fight}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:My grandmother used to tell stories about our brave ancestors. I'm interested in learning more about them. She would say they weren't afraid to face any challenge. I'm sorry for not paying more attention to her stories when I was a child. Sometimes, I feel like I could faint when I think about the difficulties they faced. There was a particular tale about a drum that called the tribe to battle. Their productivity in hard times was outstanding}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The new security system had a bug, which caused all the monitors to display a strange cartoon. It was afraid of crashing completely. The IT specialist was interested in finding the root cause. He said the system was under too much pressure. He felt sorry to inform us that it could ruin our data. We were afraid to touch anything not to make it worse. It was a very delicate situation}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A City Under Threat[/center]\nCommander: Our people are hostage. We are afraid to make a move that could ruin them.\nSoldier: I understand, sir. But we are also afraid of doing nothing. This constant pressure is unbearable.\nCommander: I'm sorry to put you in this situation. I'm interested to know if the bug in their communication system can be identified.\nSoldier: We are interested in finding a weakness. Our loyalty to our homeland is absolute. We would never let our people remain in this cage.\nCommander: Cool! I'm sorry for making you wait. Take this drum; it's an inspiration from our ancestors. We must take a decisive measure instantly. Afterward, we will see if our productivity has yielded a spectacular outcome. Even if you feel faint, keep going!"
  },
  {
    "lesson": 127,
    "text1":
        "{r:The night was dark, and a strange mystery happened. I stood by my window and saw the old building's roof explode. The tremendous noise hit me instantly, making my chest move fast. I noticed the earthquake shake the entire place. My neighbor said he had also heard the glass break from his house. We both agreed it was a fascinating, but scary, event}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Later that morning, the police began their investigation. I saw a police man shave his beard thoroughly before leaving the station. He was known for his reliability. I heard him telling his colleague that they wouldn't tolerate any false information. I also noticed him taking the responsibility of the entire case. It was fascinating to watch his dedication; he was always very precise in his actions}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The pressure was strong. I felt my anxiety rise as the minutes passed by. We were waiting for a cab that seemed to vanish. I saw my friend chewing his lip, a clear sign of his nervous state. He found the puzzle of this delay hard to understand. I heard him talking about the transport system's lack of reliability. It was sheer trouble}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:During our forest walk, we came across a terrific sight. I saw an enormous mushroom growing out of the ground, almost as tall as a small tree. It was truly fascinating. My friend instantly pulled out his phone to capture the moment. A bit more, we heard a tremendous noise. We ran to the coast and saw a whale jump from the water, then dive down into the sea. It was a spectacular display}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Urban Observations[/center]\nMe: Did you see that car's wheel explode a few distance away instantly?\nFriend: No! I only heard the tremendous sound. I was busy watching that barber shave his customer's head so thoroughly.\nMe: Wow. I noticed him carrying a large amount of tools earlier. His reliability is outstanding.\nFriend: Indeed. I also noticed the cab driver talking to himself. He seemed very mysterious.\nMe: Haha. I feel like we're always finding new puzzles in this city. Like, I saw someone eating an entire fresh mushroom yesterday. It was a bit scary.\nFriend: That's sheer madness! I don't think I could tolerate that. But it's fascinating what you see if you just pay attention."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 128,
    "text1":
        "{r:Feeling a strange shaking, she looked at the window. The earthquake started suddenly, shaking her house. Not knowing what to do, she tried to grab her child. Her sibling ran downstairs quickly, shouting for help. Outside, the tremendous noise of the explosion added to the chaos. Having experienced earthquakes before, she knew the danger was real. She covered her head, praying to stay safe}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:An aspiring entrepreneur, he was always interested in finding new ways to make money. Having recently developed a special liquid that could heal old wounds, he hoped for success. He dreamed of a glorious future. He spent hours upstairs, working on his plans, often forgetting to eat. Sitting at his desk, he would draw cartoons in his notebook, finding inspiration in simple things. He was fascinated by the idea of helping people}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The little rabbit, living in the backyard, was very clever. It often ran around, trying to find food. One day, feeling hungry, it jumped closer to the fence. Seeing a small hole, it decided to enter the neighbor's garden. It moved its nose, smelling the fresh grass. This rabbit was always looking for new adventures, not afraid of exploring the world}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:During our forest walk, we came across a terrific sight. I saw an enormous mushroom growing out of the ground, almost as tall as a small tree. It was truly fascinating. My friend instantly pulled out his phone to capture the moment. A little more, we heard a tremendous noise. We ran to the coast and saw a whale jump from the water, then dive into the sea. It was a spectacular display}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]A Family Affair[/center]\nMy sibling and I were cleaning the backyard. Feeling tired, I sat down. 'I saw a rabbit run through the garden yesterday,' I said, wiping my forehead.\n'Really? I noticed our entrepreneur cousin looking at it with a fascinated look,' my sibling replied, putting a brush on the ground.\n'He's probably interested in using it for some experiment,' I joked, standing up slowly. 'Remember when he tried to create a liquid that would heal everything? Having seen the explosion it caused, I don't think I can ever give him my consent for such things again.'\n'True,' my sibling laughed, 'but he wants to gain glory! Yesterday, having a fever, he still worked on his computer upstairs. I saw him tackling a complex puzzle. He's so dedicated.' I felt my hip start to ache."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 129,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our family's five-day trip started with a visit to an old stone castle. The castle walls were strong and gray. Our tour guide told us about its ancient origin. We had to inspect every room thoroughly, looking for hidden paths. Walking through the dark rooms, we noticed old weapon displays. It was a fascinating place, drawing visitors from worldwide locations}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Later, we visited a busy fish market. A friendly trader called out to us, offering fresh seafood. I saw him fry some fish in a large pan. We bought a basket of seafood, paying with the local currency. My friend was interested in the cooking methods there. He said it was a terrific example of simple, good food}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:For breakfast, we decided to make pancakes. My mother used a special pancake technique. While she was cooking, I looked out the window. I saw a tall sunflower growing in our garden, its yellow head facing the sun. My sister came downstairs, putting on her lipstick. She wore a bright dress that reminded me of a rainbow of colors. We ate our pancakes, feeling happy and full}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Our next journey took us to a beautiful waterfall view. The sound of the waterfall was tremendous. The forest path was narrow, and we noticed a sign for disabled access. It was important to provide good travel means for everyone. We sat by the river, listening to the water flow, thinking about the origin of such natural beauty. We even saw a small rabbit drinking from the river}.",
    "text5":
        "[center]Town Discoveries[/center]\nMe: I noticed the new town center has a very modern design. \nFriend: Yes, that's cool. The bus stop there is quite unique too. It's a good example of public transport planning. \nMe: True. I also heard about a new book store that sells worldwide literature.\nFriend: Oh, that's fascinating! I hope they have some cook books. I want to learn to fry seafood perfectly. I need a good fry pan. And maybe a recipe book for pancakes!\nMe: Haha, sounds like a plan! I'm just happy we're able to explore our city's hidden gems. It's a puzzle how much we don't know about our own place."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 130,
    "text1":
        "{r:The baker dreamed of his own shop. Having worked for many years in a large company, he wanted his own space. He had a plan for a delicious strawberry cake, a recipe of his own origin. He spent hours creating the perfect dough, working by himself in his small kitchen. A friend of his, a flower dealer, would always tell him that his cakes were the best. This dream was a constant reminder of his goal}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Having decided to start his own business, he began the preliminary work. He wanted to open a new restaurant that would comprise seafood and pancake dishes. The scene was set. He needed to find a good location and confirm all the necessary regulations. A cousin of his, an architect, helped him design the construction plan. He would often tell him that having your own place was a great achievement. He learned much about business by himself}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:At the market, a food dealer was selling garlic and other vegetables. I noticed a strange toy vessel on his table that he made on his own. A customer of his asked him about the origin of the garlic. The dealer explained properly, giving informative details. The surrounding area was full of people, all trying to buy the best products. I watched them talking about the daily prices, feeling happy to be there}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I was sent to inspect a building that was located near the old castle. I needed to confirm if the construction was done properly. It was a task I had to do on my own. The surrounding area was quiet, and the only noise was the wind. The first report was not good, and I felt the heavy responsibility on my shoulders. I needed to make my own decision about the future of the project, even though it was a difficult one}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:Having cooked my own dinner by myself, I sat down to eat. It was a simple meal of fried seafood and garlic. Suddenly, a dog of theirs ran into my kitchen, barking loudly. It was a playful dog, but I was surprised. Then, a neighbor of mine came to the door, looking for his dog. He apologized thoroughly for the disturbance. Having finished his business in the city, he was going back home. He noticed my own plate of seafood and smiled}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 131,
    "text1":
        "{r:The old house was full of secrets. Neither the lower floor nor the upper floor was safe. My friend believed that a beast lived there. It was an inappropriate thought, but he felt it. We needed to disclose the truth. Both of us felt a strange fear. We were not sure if we were eligible to enter}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:We decided to confront the mystery. We walked to the door. Neither of us spoke a word. I knew that this would be a difficult task. Either my friend or I would have to lead. We had to justify our presence there. We did not want to interfere with anything dangerous. The very air felt nasty}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Inside, the scene was strange. An old pot with its lid was on the table. Both the pot and the lid were made of old metal. We saw a lion's picture on the wall. It was an inaccurate drawing, but it made me think of a real beast. We looked for any confirmation of our theory. There was a clear distinction between fantasy and reality}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:We found an old tire in a dark corner. It was flat. Neither this tire nor any other tire was part of the mystery. It was just a random thing. We needed to disclose what we saw to the police. Both of us felt a strange need to report the condition of the house. It seemed to suffer from poverty and neglect}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:The police officer gave us a confirmation. Neither the beast nor the strange events were real. He said that our thoughts were inappropriate. We could either believe him or continue to think about the mystery. Both of us decided to trust his words. It was hard to justify our earlier fears. We left the house, leaving the old pot and its lid behind}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 132,
    "text1":
        "{r:My room was a whole mess. It seemed inevitable that I would have to clean it. Every toy was on the floor. All my clothes were on the chair. There was a compelling need to start. However, I felt extremely lazy}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:I decided to bring some things to the dustbin. I needed an order for the cleaning. Each thing had a specific place. I put all the paper in one pile. My hands were sensitive to the dust. I tried to resolve the problem of too much stuff. There was no interfering from my family, thankfully}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:An ordinary spider made a web in the corner. It was a small piece of nature in my room. I did not want to hurt it. My cat, who was fierce, tried to jump on the spider. I had to interfere and stop her. Her fur was very soft. This was an inevitable delay}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:I spoke to my father about the spider. He was an ordinary man, but he had good advice. He told me that every creature had its place. He said I could attach a piece of straw to a stick and move the spider outside. His vocal advice was always helpful. He did not like severe confrontation}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:I followed my father's order. I found a straw and a stick. With accuracy, I moved the spider. It was a small victory. My whole room felt cleaner. I hoped to enhance this feeling every day. All the problems were gone. It was a simple habit that would make my life better}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 133,
    "text1":
        "{r:The new project was exciting to all the workers at first. But there was an unfair feeling about the first task. Its difficulty was distracting. Every person felt a bit confused. Anyway, the whole team was interested in the transformation it promised. It seemed compelling and we should do our best}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The work was very tiring. Every small noise from outside was distracting. It seemed unfair to impose such a strict rule about silence. One man felt very annoyed. He thought it was an annoying situation. All of us focused on our chunk of work}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:Suddenly, the news came: a hurricane was going to invade the city. The whole town was shocked. This was truly frightening news. People felt frightened and confused. The jungle near the city was very dense. We knew the storm would be severe. It was hard to have any positive thoughts}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:We needed to find a solution. An ordinary man tried to help everybody. He had been a soldier and wore boots. He said we should not deceive anyone. He was calming, not frightening. He emphasized the merit of working together. All the people listened to his vocal opinion. He did not like severe confrontation}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:The plan was discussed. Its logic was convincing. People felt convinced that this was the right way. All of us asked about our eligibility to help. We knew the transformation would be slow, but inevitable. Every person wanted to do their part. We were amazed by the cooperation. They even had some beans for food, a small fraction of what was needed. There was no interference with their actions}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 134,
    "text1":
        "{r:The old tower stood on a high peak. Its stone walls looked very strong. The wind blew constantly around it. There was a strange feeling in the air. People often felt a small dip in their mood when they stood near it. It seemed crucial to understand its history}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:One day, a curious creature appeared. It had long feathers and a bright eyebrow. It moved very slowly at first, then it started to run fast. Its eyes looked deeply into your soul. The creature did not seem scared. It seemed holy to some, but others felt a sense of disorder near it}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The creature made a strange sound. It felt like a command to all who heard it. Its power literally filled the whole space. People listened carefully. Some felt unstable, others felt a sudden enhancement of their senses. The sound stopped quickly}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:After that, a small riot started. People were confused and acted nervously. This disorder grew constantly. The police had to devote themselves to keeping the peace. They worked very hard. There was a clear need for an enhancement of control. The situation felt very serious}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:The mayor decided it was a crucial moment. He offered a discount on food for all the town's folk. He hoped this would calm them. His command was given directly. Some people who looked like twins helped him. Two people were severely injured in the earlier chaos. This experience taught them a lesson about life}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 135,
    "text1":
        "{r:The old house was so quiet. Its history seemed so mysterious. A family hoped to receive a strange inheritance. It was a risky idea, but they felt a compelling need. They had heard stories of hidden silver and old secrets. They hoped to find a treasure inside}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Inside, they found a small, old map. It was such an ancient map! It showed a place in the jungle. The task was so hard that it seemed like a defeat before they started. They knew they needed an ally. They often shared a quick glance, trying to understand the inner and outer meanings}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The family decided to invite their personnel to help. They were such brave people! Every person agreed to devote themselves to the journey. They packed many things, including bags of corn. They hoped for an abundancy of food in the jungle. It was such a long way to go}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The path through the jungle was so dense. It was such a difficult walk that they felt very tired. The sun was so hot that their skin felt like marble. They saw a lot of tall crops. A small creature with pink feathers flew constantly near them. The creature made a strange sound}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:They knew they had to bind themselves to the task. It was so important. They saw a great swing hanging from a tree. The sight of it felt so hopeful. They felt they could finally embrace the end of their difficult journey. But their leader gave a command to move forward. Overall, this journey was such a memory they would never forget}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 136,
    "text1":
        "{r:The new essay was quite long. It was rather a difficult topic for me. I felt a bit anxious about finishing it in time. My friend said the instructions were pretty clear, but I found them fairly confusing. I knew I had to work hard}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:I searched for information on many channels. The pace of my work needed to be rapid. It was quite a lot of data to read. I found diverse opinions, which made the task rather interesting. I focused on the specific flavor of arguments that helped my idea}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:I worked late into the night. The city lights shone smoothly below. My thoughts were quite clear. I was not absent from my purpose. It was pretty important to finish. I hoped my efforts would cause something great}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The day of the delivery came. I felt fairly confident. My essay was ready. I stood before the giant screen. The presentation was quite impressive, I thought. The questions afterwards were rather difficult, but I answered them well}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:After some days, an award ceremony took place. I was there, feeling quite relaxed. The atmosphere was pretty good. My name was called! It was quite a surprise. My essay had won! This was not a disappointing result at all. It was quite an adventure. The message was urgent to share. I felt happy and looked at the green valley below}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 137,
    "text1":
        "{r:The new task was much harder than I expected. I felt a little more anxious every day. The work seemed incomplete at first. There was an absence of clear instructions. They needed to assign new roles. I knew that the sooner I started, the easier it would be}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:I decided to find some entertainment. It seemed no better to stay so focused on the task. I needed to restore my mind. A friend told me about a special place. He said it was an extraordinary valley with a calming atmosphere}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:This valley seemed much farther than I thought. A vacation there would be quite nice. The longer I thought, the more excited I became. This was a temporary solution to my stress. I hoped the weather would be getting better and better}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The valley was quite beautiful. The trees were far taller than the buildings. The air felt a lot cleaner there. I found a stable house, even a sofa in the garden. This permanent feeling of peace was truly impressive. I felt I had to live a simple life there}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:I heard news of a treaty being discussed. It was said that the prior testimony was a bit fake. A very talkative leader spoke to the crowd. He asked: Is there any better way to solve this problem? His rank was very high. The assault on truth was getting clearer and clearer. We hoped the land would yield a good result. It felt like heaven would help}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 138,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our town was once very wealthy. Life here was known for its simplicity. But things began to change. People didn't live with such ease any longer. A powerful storm brought great destruction. The old ways seemed to be no more}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Many felt the future was unstable. Some advocates tried to help, but it was so hard. They didn't even know how to proceed. Their efforts seemed unable to last very long. A small dispute started among the leaders. It felt like a truly disappointing time}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:The leaders worked hard to overcome the problems. They faced every encounter bravely. They decided to retain their unity. One plan was for a special resort to offer a discount for affected families. It was a remarkable idea, and people even discussed it at length}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:Not everyone could overcome their difficulties. One old woman couldn't even see any more; she was blind. She couldn't read any longer. Her tongue was also weak, and she spoke very slowly. She needed an incentive to keep going}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:Her children decided to sue the company that caused the destruction. It was a bold assignment. They hoped to find shelter for their mother. They presented facts to the court. They would no longer accept the current situation. They knew even the smallest efforts could make us achieve something}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 139,
    "text1":
        "{r:The news came suddenly. It was quite a confusing report. Even though the facts seemed clear, the situation was illogical. A small bunch of people gathered, trying to think about what happened. They couldn't detect any simple truth}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The decision felt temporarily unfair. Although some argued, the choice was permanently made. It came from a remote boundary, a place far away. Despite the growing controversy, the leaders did not withdraw their statement. They seemed very proud}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:People needed to know the raw truth. They felt an urgent need for justice. Even though the truth was dangerous, they wanted to testify. They wanted to prove that the man was innocent. In spite of the danger, they felt it was their duty}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:There was mutual support in the town. Although the problems were many, people helped each other. They prepared food, mostly rice. They talked about the relevant facts. Despite having little, they shared everything they had}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:A new threat began to arise. It was like a bullet moving slowly. Even though the main dispute seemed calm, a new controversy began. People didn't feel safe any longer. They knew they had to overcome this}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 140,
    "text1":
        "{r:Our region faced a new challenge. There was a noticeable increase in emissions from nearby factories. The air didn't feel pure any longer. Environmental groups began to protest. They planned a comprehensive study, in case the situation got worse. They wanted to prove the innocence of nature}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:The deer in the forest were vulnerable. Their habitat was shrinking. We knew they might migrate if things didn't improve. As a result, local volunteers created special areas of shelter, in case the animals needed to flee quickly. We added more food in case they become hungry}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:To deal with the problem, the community decided to sustain their efforts. They needed to find a steady way forward. One farmer offered his own land for a new project. We put a big pile of materials there, in case we needed them for construction}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:However, a wave of corruption appeared. Some officials tried to split the funds for their own benefit. People felt angry. They planned a protest meeting, in case of any unfairness from the local authorities. There was a huge pile of proof collected against them}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:Despite the difficulties, there was still joy. Children made toys from leather pieces. They followed their old family customs. We stored some extra toys in a box, in case a child lost his favorite. This increased the efficiency of their happiness}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 141,
    "text1":
        "{r:A new chapter in our lives began. We decided to explore a remote land. Our fate was uncertain. We knew we wouldn't succeed unless we worked together. We packed enough food to consume for weeks, as long as the weather remained stable}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:Rules were important for our safety. We couldn't move forward unless we found a clear trace of the path. Each person wore a uniform, as long as it was available. We learned to derive strength from our challenges. We wouldn't give up unless it became completely impossible}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:We had an ongoing task: crossing a difficult terrain. We knew we had to be careful. A hidden rock could make us sink. Even though the way was tough, we continued. We wouldn't fire a rifle unless we faced a direct threat. We tried to avoid any contest with wild animals}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:We found an infant animal, lost and small. It seemed to resemble a tiny fox. We knew we couldn't touch it unless its mother was not there at all. We built a small tent for our temporary shelter, as long as it was needed. We valued our privacy during the long nights}.",
    "text5":
        "{r:Our plan required sophisticated systems and efficient methods. We had to prepare a contract for our shared responsibilities. There was a feeling of dependence on each other. We would survive as long as we didn't fall for any trick. We even brought extra fabric for repairs}."
  },
  {
    "lesson": 142,
    "text1":
        "{r:The old town was in a desperate situation. People were unaware of the hidden problems below them. As the workers began to operate, they tried to uncover ancient ruins. They needed to act promptly}.",
    "text2":
        "{r:As they continued digging, they had to undergo many challenges. They tried not to overlook any small detail. Then, they found something remarkable. It was a thin blade of metal. Since it was so old, they knew it was special}.",
    "text3":
        "{r:This blade could depict a forgotten heritage. It was part of a longer sequence of historical events. We hoped it would be important for all. As the scientists examined the object, they felt a strange comfort. They needed to prove its legitimate origin}.",
    "text4":
        "{r:The discovery quickly became a legacy for the entire nation. Since it was so important, they had to cope with intense public interest. As the news spread, the consumption of related articles rose sharply. They knew the public opinion was high}.",
    "text5":
